1
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:15,599
Fatma!

2
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:27,679
Stop... stop...
What is happening here?

3
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:29,799
What is happening?

4
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:31,919
Osman Bey.

5
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:33,879
Osman Bey, right.

6
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:37,279
You will tell me what is happening.

7
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:39,159
Or I will kill you!

8
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:44,159
Be careful where you aim your arrow, Osman Bey!

9
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:48,159
You are the one at the tip of my sword, Hatun.

10
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:50,559
You should be careful first.

11
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:55,399
Father stop! Stop!

12
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:00,319
Stop! Don't, father!

13
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:03,879
Brother, drop your sword!
-My Bey...

14
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:11,159
Father, it was not Esenbike
Hatun who raided the tribe!

15
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:29,479
Holofira... Holofira...

16
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:32,959
Are you alright?
-We are...

17
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:34,359
We are, don't worry.

18
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:36,919
It was Ulugan, father.

19
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:39,839
Esenbike Hatun saved our lives.

20
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:44,679
If it wasn't for Esenbike Hatun, no
one could have survived in the tribe.

21
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:47,399
Is that so..

22
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:54,919
So she protected you, huh?

23
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:59,399
We arrived on time and wanted to save everyone.

24
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:02,879
I sent Sargun after that traitor Ulugan.

25
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:06,119
Osman Bey, don't worry.

26
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:10,399
He will pay for what he did for sure.

27
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,719
This is nothing yet, Ulugan.

28
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:23,959
Osman and his stupid herd behind him...

29
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,159
...will suffer in agony at the
tip of the sword of Esenbike...

30
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:30,119
...whom they see as their savior.

31
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:33,279
They will beg for their lives.

32
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,919
Kayi's people always show...

33
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:45,519
...gratitude to those who
approach with goodness...

34
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:50,639
...and furor to those who come with evilness.

35
00:04:50,640 --> 00:04:53,279
Don't worry.

36
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:56,839
They are badly injured...

37
00:04:57,960 --> 00:05:01,199
They haven't been in peace
for a long time, Osman Bey.

38
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:05,679
Ending this hardship, poverty...

39
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:08,319
...and landlessness...

40
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:11,319
...depends on you.

41
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:20,079
Tomorrow is the last day for you to pay the tax.

42
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:25,239
Come and say yes to me...

43
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:29,359
...and we'll forget about the tax.

44
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:33,679
We will be relatives then, not enemies.

45
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:38,919
Let us draw strength from
each other, not blood and death.

46
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:46,719
Esenbike Hatun!

47
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:55,159
Where is Ulugan?

48
00:05:56,720 --> 00:05:58,999
We killed some of his nokers but...

49
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:01,199
...we lost Ulugan's trails.

50
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:13,759
Surely the day will come when he will
kneel before me and beg for his life...

51
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:17,319
...and lose his life while begging.

52
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:22,719
Who will kneel before whom
and who will beg for mercy..

53
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:26,119
Time will show us that.

54
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:33,359
We'll meet of course.

55
00:06:34,400 --> 00:06:36,199
We'll meet at iftar tonight.

56
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:38,879
We will.

57
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:43,079
I have come to the frontiers
with thousands of nokers.

58
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:46,199
And thousands more are on their way here.

59
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:53,919
If you stand next to me...

60
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:58,039
...no one in this world can defeat you.

61
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:01,999
Are we going to be relatives or enemies?

62
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:04,279
Think carefully, Osman Bey.

63
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:29,959
We will follow Esenbike.

64
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:31,719
Okay my Bey..

65
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:36,799
You are swinging your sword in vain, Bala.

66
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:39,359
We both know that you cannot kill me.

67
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:41,267
What I will do to you
will make you suffer even more, Sofia.

68
00:07:41,279 --> 00:07:43,079
You will
give my daughter to me!

69
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:44,599
You cannot escape from me!

70
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:10,519
We're retreating. Come on.

71
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:13,999
Sofia.

72
00:08:24,320 --> 00:08:27,959
We'll see Ulugan, Sargun.
I have things to tell him.

73
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:31,959
We should watch our back then, mother.

74
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:34,719
Nokers!

75
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:38,599
You join the ones coming
after us and wait together.

76
00:08:39,558 --> 00:08:42,639
Whoever comes from the tribes, we should know!

77
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,959
-And nobody will pass beyond here.
-As you order, my Bey!

78
00:09:06,120 --> 00:09:08,959
My Bey, where are you going?

79
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:14,719
-My Bey, did we lose the tribe?
-Don't worry.

80
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:17,199
The tribe is safe.

81
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:20,999
Ulugan and Esenbike are playing against us.

82
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,919
Now it's time to ruin their game.

83
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:30,479
My Bey, do you think their
capturing Ulugan was just a game?

84
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:36,839
Time to go!

85
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:50,879
-They're coming!
-Damn it, Hristo.

86
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:54,359
-Where are the watchmen?
-Near the horses. A little ahead!

87
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:57,039
Sofia!

88
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:04,039
You can't go anywhere. You
have to give me my daughter!

89
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:13,879
They are standing ready for us, my Bey.

90
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:17,839
Esenbike is predicting all of our moves.

91
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:19,839
And she keeps raising obstacles.

92
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:23,839
No matter what they do to
stop us, we will break them.

93
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:26,719
But we'll do it quietly.

94
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:32,919
Come on, prepare your arrows.

95
00:10:36,880 --> 00:10:38,759
Release.

96
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:51,079
My Bey, they're running away to inform Esenbike.

97
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:54,119
-Ride and follow them!
-Let's go.

98
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:23,439
Soldiers, stall them!

99
00:11:33,280 --> 00:11:35,599
I said you can't go anywhere, Sofia.

100
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:38,999
You'll die before you meet
your daughter, huh, Bala?

101
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:42,639
-We'll see that when it's time.
-Soldiers, attack!

102
00:11:42,800 --> 00:11:44,919
Come on, brothers!

103
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:15,919
Well..

104
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:21,039
You were going to inform your master, huh?

105
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:23,999
They'll do it if they keep standing, brother.

106
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:26,279
But they won't be able to.

107
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:48,799
The Righteous!

108
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:58,319
We'll continue on foot.

109
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:05,519
Osman took the bait.

110
00:13:05,720 --> 00:13:10,959
Now he's resting quietly in his
tribe and healing his wounds.

111
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:14,999
If Osman is quiet,

112
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:18,279
...he must be planning a storm.

113
00:13:19,880 --> 00:13:22,919
But I won't wait for the storm to break out.

114
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:25,119
I'll do what I do.

115
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:29,399
I don't want any mistakes
or disobedience, Ulugan.

116
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:35,359
All the nokers and
commanders in the frontiers...

117
00:13:35,680 --> 00:13:38,159
...won't do anything without my permission.

118
00:13:38,240 --> 00:13:40,239
-Otherwise...
-Otherwise?

119
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:44,319
Otherwise what, Esenbike Hatun?

120
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:47,439
Otherwise what?

121
00:13:51,760 --> 00:13:56,319
Finish your words so I can say mine.

122
00:13:58,160 --> 00:14:03,439
Otherwise the ones making
mistakes will be punished with blood.

123
00:14:24,760 --> 00:14:27,719
-Good job, hatun. Come on.
-Come on.

124
00:14:58,560 --> 00:15:00,599
Sofia

125
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:08,599
Sofia!

126
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:25,999
The soil will be watered
with your blood, Shahzade.

127
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:29,479
Only Allah knows that.

128
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,079
You're struggling in vain, Bala.

129
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:09,519
Halime will never remember you.

130
00:16:09,520 --> 00:16:11,639
We'll see what when it's time, Sofia.

131
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:02,759
Gonca!

132
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:15,479
-Gonca, are you alright? -I'm fine.

133
00:17:15,520 --> 00:17:18,159
You never leave me alone!

134
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:20,959
-Always, always. Let's go.
-Let's go.

135
00:17:26,839 --> 00:17:28,919
You have to speak.

136
00:17:36,640 --> 00:17:38,399
Sofia!

137
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:48,559
Hristo, we are retreating!

138
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,879
Sofia!

139
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:02,999
Keep running, Sofia!

140
00:18:04,720 --> 00:18:07,279
You're going to bring Halime to me.

141
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:11,479
-Are you alright?
-Are you alright?

142
00:18:11,480 --> 00:18:13,719
I'm fine. She thinks she's escaped.

143
00:18:13,920 --> 00:18:17,319
-But we'll follow her like her shadow. Come on.
-Bala Hatun.

144
00:18:19,480 --> 00:18:22,839
Thanks to Allah, I found you.
Osman Bey is waiting for you.

145
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:35,399
-What's the matter, mother?
-Ulugan attacked our tribe.

146
00:18:35,960 --> 00:18:38,639
-What?
-Help us, my Allah.

147
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:40,879
What happened?

148
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:43,679
Esenbike repelled Ulugan.

149
00:18:43,840 --> 00:18:46,759
She's coming to dinner.
Osman Bey is waiting for me.

150
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:51,359
Alaaddin, Gonca. You go after Sofia.

151
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:53,119
I'm going to the tribe.

152
00:18:53,320 --> 00:18:55,439
We'll watch their every step, mother.

153
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:59,399
We'll never come back before we
find a lead about my sister. Don't worry.

154
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:01,279
Be careful, Alaaddin Ali.

155
00:19:01,480 --> 00:19:05,199
-Go now.
-As you order, mother. Let's go, Gonca.

156
00:19:05,920 --> 00:19:07,879
Come on, we're going to the tribe.

157
00:19:11,760 --> 00:19:13,599
Come on.

158
00:19:14,800 --> 00:19:16,239
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

159
00:19:16,360 --> 00:19:22,719
You will punish with blood
whoever makes a mistake, huh?

160
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:25,159
You heard me, Ulugan.

161
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:08,959
My Bey, we killed all the watching nokers.

162
00:20:13,240 --> 00:20:15,039
Once again, they didn't surprise me.

163
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:20,639
All the demons are united
and marching to one target.

164
00:20:22,040 --> 00:20:26,479
I'm Ulugan, one of the greatest
commanders of Mongolians.

165
00:20:27,080 --> 00:20:33,799
Our mighty Khan Olcaytu set a target for me.

166
00:20:33,880 --> 00:20:35,799
I'll follow him.

167
00:20:36,080 --> 00:20:37,239
I will.

168
00:20:37,760 --> 00:20:41,039
To some point, though.

169
00:20:44,640 --> 00:20:46,839
Say what you have to say, Ulugan.

170
00:20:46,960 --> 00:20:49,799
I'm telling you to hurry up, Esenbike Hatun.

171
00:20:50,560 --> 00:20:54,079
Before I defeat Osman with my sword

172
00:20:54,280 --> 00:20:58,679
...you should finish the game you call peace.

173
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:02,639
No. You have to be patient, Ulugan.

174
00:21:04,440 --> 00:21:08,199
You'll swing your sword Osman only for a game.

175
00:21:08,840 --> 00:21:12,759
You'll force him to ally with me.

176
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:17,279
When Osman has to have an agreement with me.

177
00:21:17,280 --> 00:21:20,879
When Osman has to have an agreement with me,

178
00:21:21,240 --> 00:21:24,119
...all his people will see me as the savior...

179
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:29,239
...and all Turkmen Beys appearing
before me will show respect to me.

180
00:21:32,640 --> 00:21:35,279
We'll get Osman isolated.

181
00:21:35,640 --> 00:21:42,159
When all of our army marching to the
borders of Kayi now arrive in the frontiers,

182
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:47,839
...then we will hit him hard.

183
00:21:52,720 --> 00:21:54,839
You demon.

184
00:21:55,440 --> 00:22:00,839
When she approached us with
the peace, she had an evil plan.

185
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:06,799
Yes. We'll make them pay
for getting united against Turks.

186
00:22:07,920 --> 00:22:11,759
I will ruin Esenbike's evil plans.

187
00:22:17,480 --> 00:22:20,359
My lady, we should examine your wound.

188
00:22:20,680 --> 00:22:24,119
You should have take measures
before the wound was opened.

189
00:22:24,120 --> 00:22:26,199
You should have brought more soldiers.

190
00:22:26,200 --> 00:22:30,559
Not to get exposed, I tried...
-Shut up, Hristo!

191
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:35,439
Bala survived today.

192
00:22:36,760 --> 00:22:39,199
Both Osman and Bala..

193
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:41,879
...will fall into my clutches again.

194
00:22:42,280 --> 00:22:44,359
Come on, faster.

195
00:22:44,960 --> 00:22:47,639
We're going to Akhisar.

196
00:23:00,800 --> 00:23:02,759
Keep running, you snake.

197
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:07,759
When we meet my sister,
we will take care of you.

198
00:23:07,880 --> 00:23:09,239
Come on.

199
00:23:19,760 --> 00:23:22,319
Look at our situation in our own land.

200
00:23:22,720 --> 00:23:24,959
I don't know if there is even worse.

201
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:34,679
Salute Esenbike Hatun.

202
00:24:02,160 --> 00:24:03,839
Welcome.

203
00:24:04,520 --> 00:24:06,719
You've honored me, Beys.

204
00:24:06,880 --> 00:24:09,479
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

205
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:14,839
I invited you here to say..

206
00:24:15,680 --> 00:24:19,879
...the oppression is over.

207
00:24:22,320 --> 00:24:29,039
You'll be embraced by the
mercy of the Great Ilkhanid State.

208
00:24:30,440 --> 00:24:34,279
How will that happen while Ulugan
is storming around, Esenbike Hatun?

209
00:24:34,560 --> 00:24:39,679
Ulugan is just a tiny bit
compared to the Ilkhanid State.

210
00:24:40,960 --> 00:24:43,399
He will definitely be punished.

211
00:24:44,280 --> 00:24:47,799
What do you want from us then, Esenbike Hatun?

212
00:24:48,120 --> 00:24:53,759
I saved the family of Osman Bey
who you call the Protector of Frontiers...

213
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:59,639
...from Ulugan's attack a short time ago.

214
00:25:05,960 --> 00:25:12,159
Soon, he will make peace
and pledge loyalty to me.

215
00:25:14,080 --> 00:25:16,559
That's not the whole story, of course.

216
00:25:17,400 --> 00:25:19,639
He'll either pay taxes to me...

217
00:25:20,680 --> 00:25:24,239
...or make his daughter marry my son...

218
00:25:24,600 --> 00:25:26,719
...and become a relative of mine.

219
00:25:30,840 --> 00:25:34,519
I expect Turkish Beys to pledge loyalty as well.

220
00:25:35,320 --> 00:25:37,239
Did Osman Bey...

221
00:25:39,280 --> 00:25:42,199
...accept these terms, Esenbike Hatun?

222
00:25:42,640 --> 00:25:46,119
Ilbay Bey is right. Will Osman Bey bow to you?

223
00:25:50,480 --> 00:25:51,639
As Ilbay Bey

224
00:25:52,320 --> 00:25:56,279
...accepted to stay under our wings...

225
00:25:56,840 --> 00:25:58,599
...to protect himself...

226
00:25:59,680 --> 00:26:02,799
...from burning in the fire of Ilkhanid State...

227
00:26:02,840 --> 00:26:05,919
...Osman Bey will accept our offer as well.

228
00:26:07,160 --> 00:26:08,879
I brought peace to you...

229
00:26:10,280 --> 00:26:11,719
...not war.

230
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:15,039
Now..

231
00:26:15,960 --> 00:26:17,319
...tell me.

232
00:26:18,800 --> 00:26:23,879
Whether Osman Bey is by
my side or not on this path...

233
00:26:24,480 --> 00:26:25,999
...will you stand by me?

234
00:26:31,400 --> 00:26:33,719
Your intention is good, Esenbike Hatun.

235
00:26:33,720 --> 00:26:37,159
I understand that you will not
prosper through oppression.

236
00:26:37,160 --> 00:26:39,759
Therefore, your path is my path.

237
00:26:41,240 --> 00:26:44,999
I stand with those who protect
the oppressed, not the oppressors.

238
00:26:46,800 --> 00:26:49,119
We are with you, Esenbike Hatun.

239
00:26:50,760 --> 00:26:52,359
Thank you, Beys.

240
00:26:53,400 --> 00:26:54,439
Thank you.

241
00:27:02,520 --> 00:27:04,799
Osman Bey Secret Tents

242
00:27:17,320 --> 00:27:19,119
Allah...

243
00:27:24,080 --> 00:27:25,599
-My Bey. -Orhan.

244
00:27:27,040 --> 00:27:28,759
What is the situation, my Bey?

245
00:27:28,800 --> 00:27:30,879
Just as we predicted.

246
00:27:31,680 --> 00:27:33,879
Those two traitors are working together.

247
00:27:34,200 --> 00:27:39,359
She pretended to be our savior
and had Ulugan raid our tribe, huh?

248
00:27:42,800 --> 00:27:47,159
-They will pay for what they have done.
-Don't worry.

249
00:27:47,920 --> 00:27:51,239
This will be handled today.
We will take an eye for an eye.

250
00:27:52,400 --> 00:27:54,199
What are you thinking, my Bey?

251
00:27:54,280 --> 00:28:00,079
While I waste Esenbike's time at iftar, you
will defeat the incoming reinforcement army.

252
00:28:00,200 --> 00:28:03,839
-As you order, my Bey.
-As you order, my Bey.

253
00:28:03,960 --> 00:28:06,199
But do not forget...

254
00:28:06,200 --> 00:28:10,559
...this noker unit is not like the looting ones.

255
00:28:10,920 --> 00:28:14,319
These are warrior nokers
who can fight with swords.

256
00:28:14,800 --> 00:28:16,799
We are not equal to them in numbers.

257
00:28:16,880 --> 00:28:21,799
That's why, at the end of this road,
we can become veterans or martyrs.

258
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:30,079
Being a veteran is an honour, reaching the
shahada is the highest position for us my Bey.

259
00:28:30,160 --> 00:28:35,039
Whoever comes, whether
with fire or a mace, we will...

260
00:28:35,200 --> 00:28:38,639
...fulfill the duty you gave us, God willing.

261
00:28:40,840 --> 00:28:41,959
Thank you.

262
00:28:42,960 --> 00:28:44,039
I know.

263
00:28:44,400 --> 00:28:49,679
When the end of the road is martyrdom, you
do not hesitate to sacrifice your lives.

264
00:28:51,040 --> 00:28:55,679
My Bey, we will not reveal ourselves right?
-No.

265
00:28:55,960 --> 00:29:01,559
You will disguise yourselves as those dogs
but you will make those dogs kill each other.

266
00:29:02,040 --> 00:29:07,519
We will reduce their numbers and
make Ulugan and Esenbike enemies.

267
00:29:08,200 --> 00:29:14,439
When Esenbike is attacked by Ulugan...

268
00:29:14,680 --> 00:29:19,039
...she will not be able to
swallow her bite in front of me.

269
00:29:21,880 --> 00:29:26,199
But my Bey, there is one more
thing we must be careful about.

270
00:29:26,520 --> 00:29:29,759
We should not kill each other
under the guise of those dogs.

271
00:29:29,760 --> 00:29:32,279
You are the leader of this fight, Orhan.

272
00:29:33,880 --> 00:29:37,319
You will take care of that.

273
00:29:40,200 --> 00:29:41,730
May our war be blessed.

274
00:29:41,742 --> 00:29:44,119
-Live long, my Bey.
-Thank you my Bey.

275
00:29:48,240 --> 00:29:50,439
Brother, do you have any dog disguise?

276
00:29:51,040 --> 00:29:54,119
Do you think you are funny?

277
00:29:58,280 --> 00:30:01,159
My Shahzade, find a solution to this matter.

278
00:30:02,360 --> 00:30:06,479
Otherwise, I can take this Boran's
heart out with my double swords.

279
00:30:07,960 --> 00:30:10,319
Don't be so quick to decide brother.

280
00:30:15,040 --> 00:30:16,119
Bala Hatun.

281
00:30:16,520 --> 00:30:17,599
Yes, my daughter...

282
00:30:17,600 --> 00:30:19,759
You know, that woman escaped from you...

283
00:30:20,720 --> 00:30:22,079
What will happen now?

284
00:30:22,080 --> 00:30:24,399
She is not in our hands for now, my daughter.

285
00:30:24,400 --> 00:30:27,399
But this will not stop me
from finding my Halime.

286
00:30:29,520 --> 00:30:32,319
Sofia is your enemy.

287
00:30:33,240 --> 00:30:35,999
Why do you believe her words?

288
00:30:46,640 --> 00:30:47,679
Meryem.

289
00:30:52,000 --> 00:30:53,039
Look, my daughter.

290
00:30:53,680 --> 00:30:56,559
I wrote the prayer inside
this with my own hands.

291
00:30:56,680 --> 00:30:59,079
I put this around my daughter's neck.

292
00:30:59,840 --> 00:31:01,839
My Halime is alive. I know.

293
00:31:02,240 --> 00:31:03,999
And we will find her.

294
00:31:05,360 --> 00:31:06,399
What if..

295
00:31:06,760 --> 00:31:09,439
...she is lying again to hurt you?

296
00:31:13,080 --> 00:31:14,839
Mothers can feel, Meryem.

297
00:31:15,560 --> 00:31:16,599
Who knows...

298
00:31:16,760 --> 00:31:18,479
It's so little but..

299
00:31:19,600 --> 00:31:24,559
...even I can feel it in my heart.

300
00:31:24,560 --> 00:31:28,279
If my Bala mother is saying that
Halime is alive, she must be alive.

301
00:31:29,400 --> 00:31:30,439
Right..

302
00:31:36,480 --> 00:31:37,799
My Fatma..

303
00:31:41,440 --> 00:31:43,839
My beautiful daughter, are you alright?

304
00:31:43,920 --> 00:31:44,959
Mother..

305
00:31:45,520 --> 00:31:46,759
I am afraid.

306
00:31:47,280 --> 00:31:51,399
What if they a play a game? What if they take...
-Don't you say that!

307
00:31:51,920 --> 00:31:54,599
While I, your father and
your brothers are here...

308
00:31:54,880 --> 00:31:57,959
...no one can touch you,
my beautiful-eyed daughter.

309
00:31:59,640 --> 00:32:00,679
Don't.

310
00:32:03,680 --> 00:32:04,719
Mother...

311
00:32:05,880 --> 00:32:08,719
We are preparing iftaar for our enemies

312
00:32:09,360 --> 00:32:13,399
The devil says, "Put poison
in their food, and kill them all."

313
00:32:13,520 --> 00:32:14,599
My daughter...

314
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:20,839
Responding to the tyrant's cruelty with
the same moves makes us tyrants too.

315
00:32:21,880 --> 00:32:25,879
Our path is the path of
justice. We rule with justice.

316
00:32:26,840 --> 00:32:30,239
Mother, our enemies are not like us.

317
00:32:30,320 --> 00:32:33,519
They took Halime from us
when she was a little child.

318
00:32:34,280 --> 00:32:36,759
They don't believe in right or wrong.

319
00:32:36,880 --> 00:32:40,559
We show them mercy, but they don't show us any.

320
00:32:40,560 --> 00:32:43,239
That's why Fatma, we won't be like them.

321
00:32:44,120 --> 00:32:48,359
What makes us who we are
is not our sword, but our hearts.

322
00:32:50,920 --> 00:32:54,639
With the rule of justice, we keep
the oppressed peaceful, right?

323
00:32:56,600 --> 00:33:00,039
And killing with poison is easy.

324
00:33:00,480 --> 00:33:05,399
But defeating the enemy means
making them kneel before justice.

325
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:28,719
The snake entered its nest.

326
00:33:30,080 --> 00:33:31,519
There is no other way.

327
00:33:32,920 --> 00:33:38,439
I will go into the snake's
nest to find my sister's trail.

328
00:33:42,040 --> 00:33:44,799
My Shahzade, a Byzantine unit is approaching.

329
00:33:46,840 --> 00:33:47,879
Good.

330
00:34:08,600 --> 00:34:11,119
Who are you? What do you want?

331
00:34:12,159 --> 00:34:13,759
The ruler of the frontiers...

332
00:34:15,520 --> 00:34:17,319
...the servant of Islam...

333
00:34:18,159 --> 00:34:21,638
...Osman Bey's son Shahzade Alaeddin

334
00:34:24,719 --> 00:34:28,359
So, your executioner.

335
00:34:29,880 --> 00:34:34,638
You lost your mind, Turk. You
made a mistake by facing me alone.

336
00:34:37,040 --> 00:34:38,079
Is that so?

337
00:34:39,679 --> 00:34:41,638
Now I'm scared.

338
00:34:43,480 --> 00:34:45,079
Then let's do this...

339
00:34:47,280 --> 00:34:48,759
Allah is Eternal!

340
00:34:48,760 --> 00:34:51,438
Allah is Righteous!

341
00:34:56,719 --> 00:34:58,279
I will kill you.

342
00:35:00,160 --> 00:35:02,639
I don't have a life to
give to a dog and a jackal.

343
00:35:03,320 --> 00:35:04,439
Come.

344
00:35:36,080 --> 00:35:37,439
Hide the dead.

345
00:35:38,360 --> 00:35:39,839
Put on their clothes.

346
00:35:45,840 --> 00:35:47,519
We will enter Akhisar.

347
00:35:55,520 --> 00:36:00,599
The ones coming are the
strongest nokers of the Mongol army.

348
00:36:01,160 --> 00:36:06,439
Welcoming this steel-wristed
unit is my lion-hearted son's duty.

349
00:36:06,760 --> 00:36:12,999
For your trust, I will get over the mountains
and bring that unit here, my Mother Sultan.

350
00:36:13,720 --> 00:36:17,919
May your path be open and
your mind strong, my son.

351
00:36:21,120 --> 00:36:22,159
Zolzaya.

352
00:36:23,480 --> 00:36:26,439
Have the gifts for Osman been prepared?

353
00:36:26,520 --> 00:36:29,319
As you ordered, sir. 
The carts are loaded.

354
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:37,439
We cannot go to the iftar with empty hands.

355
00:36:39,320 --> 00:36:40,439
Right Ilbay?

356
00:36:40,960 --> 00:36:42,119
Sure.

357
00:36:43,040 --> 00:36:44,239
But it's Osman.

358
00:36:45,240 --> 00:36:47,599
We will go to him with a cart full of gifts.

359
00:36:47,920 --> 00:36:50,799
But he can put poison in
front of us instead of food.

360
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:52,959
I'll go to the iftar, Ilbay.

361
00:36:54,040 --> 00:36:55,119
Not you.

362
00:37:00,240 --> 00:37:04,079
Osman's insolence has no limits, Esenbike Hatun.

363
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:07,759
Ilbay is trying to say it's
good to take precautions.

364
00:37:08,760 --> 00:37:12,999
When he has the chance, he will poison you.

365
00:37:14,120 --> 00:37:17,359
Osman's death will be beneficial
for everyone on frontiers.

366
00:37:18,200 --> 00:37:25,319
I know well what is benefical
and not beneficial for whom, Ilbay.

367
00:37:26,240 --> 00:37:28,919
I also know why you're so angry.

368
00:37:34,240 --> 00:37:35,479
Let's go, Zolzaya.

369
00:37:51,840 --> 00:37:53,759
Near Akhisar Castle

370
00:37:54,480 --> 00:37:57,919
Alps, you two will enter the castle with me.

371
00:37:58,040 --> 00:37:59,519
As you order my Shahzade.

372
00:38:02,120 --> 00:38:05,559
And you will wait with Gonca Hatun at the lodge.

373
00:38:10,080 --> 00:38:11,879
As you order my Shahzade.

374
00:38:22,760 --> 00:38:24,439
"As you order my Shahzade.", huh?

375
00:38:25,200 --> 00:38:26,639
Look at me.

376
00:38:28,040 --> 00:38:29,079
Stop there...

377
00:38:34,400 --> 00:38:35,719
Trickster Hatun...

378
00:38:37,680 --> 00:38:39,439
Why did you wear these clothes?

379
00:38:39,480 --> 00:38:41,679
Where do you think you are going?

380
00:38:41,680 --> 00:38:44,079
I will go wherever you are going. Scholar.

381
00:38:44,120 --> 00:38:45,799
No we won't do that, my Gonca.

382
00:38:46,920 --> 00:38:48,879
I said I am going into the enemy's den.

383
00:38:48,880 --> 00:38:52,559
-It's too dangerous, you can't come.
-It's dangerous, huh?

384
00:38:54,200 --> 00:38:57,399
Where did we meet, Alaeddin? Did you forget?

385
00:38:59,480 --> 00:39:01,959
I remember, I remember for sure.

386
00:39:02,560 --> 00:39:04,919
The crazy daughter of Germiyan, Gonca Hatun.

387
00:39:05,920 --> 00:39:08,399
-Crazy?
-Yes, crazy, totally crazy.

388
00:39:09,200 --> 00:39:10,239
Alaeddin.

389
00:39:11,280 --> 00:39:12,719
Calm down.

390
00:39:13,240 --> 00:39:14,639
I will come with you!

391
00:39:15,960 --> 00:39:18,279
Alright. Come then.

392
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:22,519
My Hatun's word is the last word now.

393
00:39:24,000 --> 00:39:25,039
Right...

394
00:39:28,280 --> 00:39:29,519
It won't be bad..

395
00:39:29,880 --> 00:39:31,839
We will remember the old days.

396
00:39:32,360 --> 00:39:34,839
Let it be as you said. Trickster Hatun.

397
00:39:39,640 --> 00:39:41,759
Alaeddin!

398
00:39:41,760 --> 00:39:44,439
Let's go then, Trickster Hatun, get on.

399
00:39:48,560 --> 00:39:51,799
Come on then. Everybody should be careful.

400
00:39:52,240 --> 00:39:55,679
You wait here. We may need
to send a message to my father.

401
00:39:55,880 --> 00:39:58,799
-As you order, my Bey.
-Here we go.

402
00:40:13,120 --> 00:40:14,919
Are you ready, Trickster Hatun?

403
00:40:15,440 --> 00:40:19,639
-I'm ready. Scholar.
-Here we go! May Allah help us. Let's go!

404
00:40:52,000 --> 00:40:56,679
You have many daughters and
girls. Are you still dealing with this?

405
00:40:57,000 --> 00:40:59,919
Everyone is busy, Osman. So I'm doing this.

406
00:41:00,040 --> 00:41:03,359
You invited the hatun to
iftar. We have to offer food.

407
00:41:06,920 --> 00:41:09,599
Look at me. Look.

408
00:41:10,320 --> 00:41:15,199
-Now you are the wife of Osman the Dark!
-What?

409
00:41:15,640 --> 00:41:17,799
It looks good on you, though.

410
00:41:19,320 --> 00:41:21,519
-Stop making fun of me.
-No.

411
00:41:21,840 --> 00:41:25,479
-It really looks good.
-Osman.

412
00:41:33,560 --> 00:41:37,599
I don't know if it was a good
move to invite her to iftar, but...

413
00:41:37,960 --> 00:41:40,279
...Fatma seems scared.

414
00:41:40,920 --> 00:41:44,479
No. Nobody can scare my daughter.

415
00:41:48,440 --> 00:41:54,079
I invited the enemy here so I
could know what she intends to do.

416
00:41:55,000 --> 00:41:57,839
Yes, but that hatun wants to play games.

417
00:41:58,200 --> 00:42:01,519
I'll show her how the game should be played.

418
00:42:03,280 --> 00:42:06,199
-Let's go. -Go where?

419
00:42:06,640 --> 00:42:09,959
-We need to go, Bala. They're waiting for us.
-Who?

420
00:42:10,040 --> 00:42:12,639
Oh... Fatma, Ulgen

421
00:42:13,240 --> 00:42:15,359
Check this cauldron.

422
00:42:15,520 --> 00:42:18,039
-Let's go.
-Osman, there is much to do here.

423
00:42:18,080 --> 00:42:20,879
Well... I'm taking you away.

424
00:42:21,000 --> 00:42:22,279
There is much to do.

425
00:42:22,280 --> 00:42:24,639
-We're going.
-Going where?

426
00:42:24,680 --> 00:42:26,239
You'll see when we arrive.

427
00:42:26,240 --> 00:42:28,839
-Who is waiting? -Come with me.

428
00:42:36,400 --> 00:42:37,719
My Bey.

429
00:42:38,840 --> 00:42:41,199
-We're going, huh?
-I'm taking you away!

430
00:42:52,200 --> 00:42:55,719
Won't you really tell me?
-No.

431
00:42:56,320 --> 00:42:58,759
You're really taking me away, huh?

432
00:42:59,480 --> 00:43:02,039
Well, you were so ready to come with me.

433
00:43:03,440 --> 00:43:06,879
Well... I said yes to you years ago.

434
00:43:07,000 --> 00:43:09,599
That means you are ready.

435
00:43:09,640 --> 00:43:11,759
Yes, I am.

436
00:43:13,400 --> 00:43:17,359
If you are going to death
and we're going together,

437
00:43:17,520 --> 00:43:19,119
...I will never object.

438
00:43:20,040 --> 00:43:22,839
As long as you are with me,

439
00:43:23,400 --> 00:43:27,319
...neither the path nor the death can scare me.

440
00:43:36,600 --> 00:43:39,719
Is this it? This is it.

441
00:43:52,320 --> 00:43:55,799
Osman, I'm really curious now.

442
00:43:56,040 --> 00:43:59,919
Bala, just wait. Just wait.

443
00:44:00,040 --> 00:44:03,159
Be patient. Don't be so curious.

444
00:44:07,000 --> 00:44:10,279
Look. Did you find my headscarf?

445
00:44:11,320 --> 00:44:14,159
Yes. I also found you.

446
00:44:16,200 --> 00:44:19,519
Do you know who brought it to me?
-Who?

447
00:44:33,080 --> 00:44:34,599
Alaca.

448
00:44:35,000 --> 00:44:36,439
Alaca.

449
00:44:38,680 --> 00:44:41,359
-Osman.
-Yes, Alaca.

450
00:44:44,160 --> 00:44:48,319
Alaca... My Alaca

451
00:44:59,840 --> 00:45:01,799
My Alaca.

452
00:45:02,720 --> 00:45:04,319
Osman.

453
00:45:08,920 --> 00:45:11,759
My girl. My girl.

454
00:45:13,760 --> 00:45:15,519
Well, Bala..

455
00:45:17,600 --> 00:45:19,879
I thought I lost you.

456
00:45:20,320 --> 00:45:23,439
Then Alaca brought you to me.

457
00:45:24,480 --> 00:45:28,519
After Begum wounded her that day,

458
00:45:29,160 --> 00:45:31,919
...I was afraid to hear what happened.

459
00:45:32,280 --> 00:45:36,919
-I thought I lost my girl.
-No. Don't worry.

460
00:45:38,440 --> 00:45:41,239
I made her wait to stand ready before you.

461
00:45:42,240 --> 00:45:45,439
Your girl is strong.

462
00:45:46,040 --> 00:45:47,599
Very strong.

463
00:45:48,480 --> 00:45:51,879
Yes. My Alaca, are you alright?

464
00:45:52,080 --> 00:45:55,159
-You're good.
-She's good.

465
00:45:55,400 --> 00:45:58,439
Don't worry.
She'll be even better.

466
00:45:58,520 --> 00:46:01,759
In fact, even better than before.

467
00:46:04,800 --> 00:46:05,999
Then...

468
00:46:07,000 --> 00:46:09,119
When Alaca fully recovers.

469
00:46:09,320 --> 00:46:11,999
...promise me that we will have a race.

470
00:46:12,080 --> 00:46:14,679
Oh... You say so?

471
00:46:18,200 --> 00:46:20,199
Did you hear that, Iltutan?

472
00:46:28,760 --> 00:46:32,359
Then you have my word. You have my word.

473
00:46:33,480 --> 00:46:37,919
Thanks to you, we're taking
back all what we lost, Osman.

474
00:46:39,280 --> 00:46:41,599
We'll take back our daughter too.

475
00:46:42,200 --> 00:46:44,279
And our tribe too.

476
00:46:44,920 --> 00:46:47,159
Alaaddin is following Sofia now.

477
00:46:48,160 --> 00:46:51,559
She'll definitely leave traces. Definitely.

478
00:46:52,920 --> 00:46:54,559
God willing.

479
00:46:55,680 --> 00:46:57,639
Let's go, come on.

480
00:47:10,080 --> 00:47:11,559
Bala.

481
00:47:12,200 --> 00:47:14,239
-Let's go.
-Let's go!

482
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:17,559
Come on, Alaca!

483
00:47:39,760 --> 00:47:43,799
We'll kick up a dust shortly, Boran.

484
00:47:47,720 --> 00:47:50,559
Are you ready, brother?

485
00:47:52,520 --> 00:47:55,999
Boran, I'm talking to you. Speak.

486
00:47:56,640 --> 00:47:58,759
Cerkutay Bey, I'm Yusuf.

487
00:47:59,160 --> 00:48:01,279
-Yusuf?
-Yes, Yusuf.

488
00:48:01,480 --> 00:48:03,759
Where is Boran?

489
00:48:05,320 --> 00:48:07,239
I don't know.

490
00:48:07,480 --> 00:48:11,839
Boran? Boran! Boran...

491
00:48:12,400 --> 00:48:18,559
You aren't. Where is Boran? Where is he? Boran?

492
00:48:18,680 --> 00:48:20,279
Boran

493
00:48:21,280 --> 00:48:23,319
Brother.

494
00:48:28,120 --> 00:48:30,399
What's your problem this time, Cerkutay?

495
00:48:30,680 --> 00:48:34,919
Look, brothers. I can't recognize anyone.

496
00:48:35,240 --> 00:48:38,919
If I see you in the battlefield,
I may slaughter any of you!

497
00:48:39,200 --> 00:48:40,639
Oh no.

498
00:48:40,760 --> 00:48:44,319
-How will we prevent that?
-Right, brother.

499
00:48:44,480 --> 00:48:47,599
-How can we prevent that?
-Alps.

500
00:48:53,080 --> 00:48:55,399
What will we do with them, my Shahzade?

501
00:48:55,680 --> 00:48:57,439
Wrap these around your arms.

502
00:48:57,640 --> 00:49:00,359
So you won't confuse us with the others.

503
00:49:00,800 --> 00:49:05,497
We're going to slaughter
everyone without a red rag.

504
00:49:05,509 --> 00:49:07,079
Samil.

505
00:49:07,880 --> 00:49:09,759
Brother.

506
00:49:15,040 --> 00:49:18,919
Brothers, wrap your rags tightly.

507
00:49:19,360 --> 00:49:23,799
Those without a rag around
their arms can't survive my wrath.

508
00:49:27,960 --> 00:49:30,279
Come on, alps.
-Come on.

509
00:49:34,040 --> 00:49:37,759
-Is it good?
-It looks perfect.

510
00:50:05,480 --> 00:50:08,799
My strong nokers!

511
00:50:09,840 --> 00:50:12,359
Welcome!

512
00:50:14,360 --> 00:50:19,719
We maintained order in the
eastern lands with our bloody swords!

513
00:50:20,560 --> 00:50:22,839
We spread all around.

514
00:50:23,240 --> 00:50:28,279
The western lands will be the next!

515
00:50:30,840 --> 00:50:34,039
Are you ready to....

516
00:50:35,360 --> 00:50:41,599
...make them kneel and bow to us?

517
00:50:41,760 --> 00:50:44,639
We're ready! We're ready!

518
00:50:44,720 --> 00:50:48,279
What do you promise to looters in this world?

519
00:50:48,320 --> 00:50:53,279
Blood! Blood! Blood!

520
00:51:16,640 --> 00:51:21,479
-Welcome, Esenbike Hatun.
-Welcome.

521
00:51:21,960 --> 00:51:23,999
Thank you.

522
00:51:24,400 --> 00:51:26,439
Thank you so much.

523
00:51:27,760 --> 00:51:30,479
We weren't expecting you so early.

524
00:51:37,440 --> 00:51:39,319
No problem.

525
00:51:40,000 --> 00:51:45,959
I wanted to arrive in the daylight and
hand out gifts to people before iftar.

526
00:51:48,280 --> 00:51:51,759
-Welcome, Osman Bey.
-Thanks.

527
00:51:51,840 --> 00:51:54,719
-Welcome, Osman Bey.
-Welcome, Bala Hatun.

528
00:51:58,560 --> 00:52:01,639
Coming early was a good idea, Esenbike Hatun.

529
00:52:05,080 --> 00:52:07,519
Finally, we'll get to know each other.

530
00:52:26,160 --> 00:52:28,399
Finally, Bala Hatun.

531
00:52:29,160 --> 00:52:34,079
You must have heard enough about me, though.

532
00:52:35,880 --> 00:52:40,919
We don't judge before we make sure.

533
00:52:44,600 --> 00:52:45,999
Well..

534
00:52:46,240 --> 00:52:49,039
You should rest till iftar.

535
00:52:56,840 --> 00:52:59,199
-Welcome, my Bey.
-Welcome, my Bey.

536
00:52:59,280 --> 00:53:01,359
Thank you.

537
00:53:03,840 --> 00:53:06,359
My Shahzade, Sargun and nokers are coming.

538
00:53:06,560 --> 00:53:08,679
Let them come.

539
00:53:09,400 --> 00:53:11,639
Let them come.

540
00:53:16,640 --> 00:53:19,279
-Cerkutay Bey.
-My Shahzade.

541
00:53:20,080 --> 00:53:24,359
Show us a good cryout!

542
00:53:24,680 --> 00:53:30,359
I will yell so loudly that Esenbike
Hatun will hear from our tribe.

543
00:53:30,400 --> 00:53:32,319
Alright.

544
00:53:34,800 --> 00:53:37,839
Alps, get ready.

545
00:53:47,040 --> 00:53:49,639
Attack for Ulugan!

546
00:54:01,840 --> 00:54:03,279
Ulugan.

547
00:54:03,480 --> 00:54:05,039
What are you doing?

548
00:54:05,160 --> 00:54:08,199
Ulugan will be victorious!

549
00:54:09,160 --> 00:54:11,959
You'll pay for this, Ulugan.

550
00:54:17,280 --> 00:54:21,999
You're attempting to kill me and my army, huh?

551
00:54:23,600 --> 00:54:25,399
Easy, Sargun.

552
00:54:25,480 --> 00:54:28,159
-Nokers!
-You have days to live.

553
00:54:28,320 --> 00:54:30,239
Attack!

554
00:55:49,720 --> 00:55:51,679
Die already!

555
00:56:35,720 --> 00:56:38,679
Marcus was supposed to
bring the goods. Where is he?

556
00:56:38,680 --> 00:56:40,759
He is too sick.

557
00:56:41,000 --> 00:56:43,039
So they sent me instead.

558
00:56:48,880 --> 00:56:50,159
But I'm starving.

559
00:56:50,360 --> 00:56:54,119
I want to finish this
business and eat until burst.

560
00:56:56,160 --> 00:56:58,839
Alright, you can pass. Open the gate!

561
00:57:19,360 --> 00:57:21,239
You excluded us, but...

562
00:57:21,640 --> 00:57:24,239
...Ulugan is going to make you pay for this!

563
00:57:40,520 --> 00:57:43,559
My nokers... Ulugan

564
00:57:43,840 --> 00:57:46,999
You're going to pay for this.

565
00:58:33,360 --> 00:58:36,119
-We have to go
commander.

566
00:58:36,440 --> 00:58:38,999
Come on, we're retreating!

567
00:58:46,520 --> 00:58:49,399
Two heads are better than one!

568
00:58:49,960 --> 00:58:51,759
Look how they scattered.

569
00:58:52,120 --> 00:58:56,319
Now Sargun will go and hold
onto his mother's skirt and cry.

570
00:58:57,080 --> 00:59:01,959
As long as the Turk's iron
fist and brave Alps exist...

571
00:59:02,160 --> 00:59:05,119
...they will only find peace under the ground.

572
00:59:05,360 --> 00:59:06,319
Brothers..

573
00:59:06,400 --> 00:59:09,719
...fighting like these
infidels was really difficult.

574
00:59:09,720 --> 00:59:14,159
While killing them one by one, I had a hard
time holding myself from screaming Takbir!

575
00:59:14,160 --> 00:59:16,479
Be careful, brother.

576
00:59:17,160 --> 00:59:18,279
For sure...

577
00:59:18,280 --> 00:59:22,639
For sure the day will come
when we will announce the oneness of God.

578
00:59:22,800 --> 00:59:24,639
We will shout so loudly that...

579
00:59:25,360 --> 00:59:27,959
...the whole world will hear us, God willing.

580
00:59:28,160 --> 00:59:31,359
God willing.

581
00:59:31,360 --> 00:59:33,719
My Shahzade, you're wounded.

582
00:59:33,720 --> 00:59:37,959
It's not important, Shamil. It's
not important, Alps. Let's go.

583
00:59:38,320 --> 00:59:43,119
We'll return to the tribe. Let's go there
before that Sargun dog. Let's go there...

584
00:59:43,600 --> 00:59:45,599
...and inform my Bey.

585
00:59:45,840 --> 00:59:48,359
Let's go.

586
01:00:00,040 --> 01:00:01,079
I will..

587
01:00:02,280 --> 01:00:04,439
...never accept an alliance...

588
01:00:05,320 --> 01:00:08,799
...between a Mongol and a Turk.

589
01:00:09,240 --> 01:00:10,599
I will kill them!

590
01:00:11,880 --> 01:00:14,799
Then what will we do, Ulugan?

591
01:00:16,600 --> 01:00:17,719
For now..

592
01:00:19,680 --> 01:00:21,999
...we will do what Esenbike said.

593
01:00:22,680 --> 01:00:25,079
Let Osman lower his guard first.

594
01:00:25,920 --> 01:00:28,879
Then we will put our black swords...

595
01:00:29,320 --> 01:00:33,079
...into his heart and take his heart out.

596
01:00:35,120 --> 01:00:37,599
Osman Bey Secret Tents

597
01:00:40,840 --> 01:00:44,639
Finally we met, Bala Hatun.

598
01:00:45,840 --> 01:00:47,519
It is an honor.

599
01:00:51,200 --> 01:00:56,879
You protected the lives of
our people and our loved ones.

600
01:00:57,240 --> 01:00:59,519
We are honoured, Esenbike Hatun.

601
01:01:01,000 --> 01:01:04,599
We saw and heard.

602
01:01:05,440 --> 01:01:12,479
Neither our people will spare their
gratitude nor the Beys you have invited.

603
01:01:14,200 --> 01:01:19,159
With you standing against Ulugan, it is
clear that everyone will gather around you.

604
01:01:21,840 --> 01:01:24,359
Right, Osman Bey. True.

605
01:01:25,720 --> 01:01:29,119
Those who stand by justice always gather unity.

606
01:01:30,480 --> 01:01:33,159
But you know...

607
01:01:34,880 --> 01:01:40,199
...what I really wish is to unite with you.

608
01:01:45,320 --> 01:01:50,199
My son, Sargun wanted to join the invitation.

609
01:01:50,920 --> 01:01:55,679
But he went to welcome the reinforcement units.

610
01:01:56,280 --> 01:01:58,919
So the reinforcement units have arrived, huh?

611
01:02:00,480 --> 01:02:03,519
Where are your Shahzades, Osman Bey?

612
01:02:05,360 --> 01:02:07,919
Our children also have their duties...

613
01:02:08,480 --> 01:02:12,279
...although those may not
be as important as your son's.

614
01:02:16,640 --> 01:02:21,159
Is this invitation for your
gratitude towards me only?

615
01:02:22,040 --> 01:02:27,719
Or will you try to make me give
up the conditions I set by saying...

616
01:02:28,280 --> 01:02:33,159
..."I cannot find the gold to pay the
tax and I will not give my daughter."?

617
01:02:33,520 --> 01:02:39,279
On the contrary, before
the time you gave us is up...

618
01:02:40,360 --> 01:02:42,759
...I will give you the tax you want tomorrow.

619
01:02:43,320 --> 01:02:44,959
That's why we invited you here.

620
01:03:15,000 --> 01:03:18,799
They are guarding Sofia's door.
Tell me. Scholar. What will we do now?

621
01:03:19,560 --> 01:03:23,839
-We will take over the shift.
-How? Where are you going Scholar?

622
01:03:33,520 --> 01:03:35,559
What are you doing here? Who are you?

623
01:03:35,880 --> 01:03:39,399
We are taking over the shift by
the order of Commander Hristo.

624
01:03:39,440 --> 01:03:41,799
There is still time before the change. Why?

625
01:03:42,160 --> 01:03:45,079
I don't know. But...

626
01:03:45,960 --> 01:03:46,999
...actually...

627
01:03:48,440 --> 01:03:50,119
...according to what I've heard..

628
01:03:51,680 --> 01:03:55,399
...damned Turks escaped from Sofia again.

629
01:03:56,680 --> 01:03:58,479
Maybe that's why.

630
01:03:59,000 --> 01:04:00,959
Don't tell anyone..

631
01:04:01,920 --> 01:04:03,759
...but both were very angry.

632
01:04:07,720 --> 01:04:08,799
The shift is yours.

633
01:04:20,280 --> 01:04:24,639
Sweet words can even bring
a snake out of its den, Hatun.

634
01:04:24,840 --> 01:04:28,999
-And your stubbornness...
-Alaeddin, be quiet! Be quiet!

635
01:04:31,240 --> 01:04:33,879
Fear, Hatun. Fear.

636
01:04:34,280 --> 01:04:36,119
Fear rules people.

637
01:04:36,360 --> 01:04:40,159
These soldiers know Sofia's
anger well. They are scared of her.

638
01:04:40,880 --> 01:04:46,439
They ran away to avoid
being punished by her anger.

639
01:04:48,000 --> 01:04:49,959
Of course they ran away.

640
01:04:49,960 --> 01:04:51,639
We broke our fast.

641
01:04:51,840 --> 01:04:53,719
We are now feeling better.

642
01:04:53,840 --> 01:04:56,959
Now answer my question, Osman Bey.

643
01:04:58,720 --> 01:05:02,759
Where did you find all that gold to pay the tax?

644
01:05:03,440 --> 01:05:05,279
Ayaz Bey...

645
01:05:06,200 --> 01:05:09,559
He will bring the gold he
obtained from the spoils...

646
01:05:09,960 --> 01:05:14,519
...from the tribes outside our borders.

647
01:05:17,160 --> 01:05:20,159
-Ayaz Bey, huh?
-Ayaz Bey, yes.

648
01:05:21,600 --> 01:05:22,759
Ayaz Bey.

649
01:05:25,760 --> 01:05:27,479
What happened, Esenbike Hatun?

650
01:05:28,320 --> 01:05:30,119
Why are you frowning?

651
01:05:31,200 --> 01:05:36,679
Shouldn't you be happy? You
will get the tax you wanted so much.

652
01:05:37,840 --> 01:05:42,839
I never thought you would
find it in such a short time.

653
01:05:44,040 --> 01:05:45,479
What makes me happy..

654
01:05:47,560 --> 01:05:49,159
...is not just the tax...

655
01:05:49,680 --> 01:05:52,999
...but the fact that there
will be peace between us.

656
01:05:53,520 --> 01:05:55,679
Good. Good.

657
01:05:56,840 --> 01:06:03,399
Tomorrow, we will pay the tax at
Guzelsu on the Karacahisar borders.

658
01:06:08,360 --> 01:06:11,679
-Can I come in, my Bey?
-Come in Orhan Bey.

659
01:06:17,400 --> 01:06:18,839
Peace be upon you.

660
01:06:19,120 --> 01:06:22,039
-Peace be upon you too.
-Peace be upon you too.

661
01:06:24,920 --> 01:06:25,959
My son

662
01:06:26,520 --> 01:06:28,879
Tell me, did you fulfill your duty?

663
01:06:28,880 --> 01:06:32,039
-Did you succeed?
-Sure.

664
01:06:35,160 --> 01:06:37,199
For sure we succeeded.

665
01:06:37,680 --> 01:06:39,439
May Allah bless you.

666
01:06:39,560 --> 01:06:41,479
May Allah bless you too, my Bey.

667
01:06:42,360 --> 01:06:45,959
-It was an important duty apparently.
-Yes.

668
01:06:47,480 --> 01:06:48,519
Right.

669
01:06:50,440 --> 01:06:53,119
It was an important duty, Esenbike Hatun.

670
01:06:57,080 --> 01:07:00,079
-My Bey can I come in? -Come in Boran.

671
01:07:03,080 --> 01:07:07,119
My Bey, Esenbike Hatun's son Sargun is here.

672
01:07:07,200 --> 01:07:10,839
Why are you keeping him outside? Let him in.

673
01:07:11,480 --> 01:07:12,519
Let him in.

674
01:07:14,000 --> 01:07:16,439
As you order, my Bey. Alps.

675
01:07:18,160 --> 01:07:19,199
Mother..

676
01:07:21,920 --> 01:07:23,639
What happened, Sargun?

677
01:07:24,880 --> 01:07:28,279
We were attacked when we
met with our reinforcement units.

678
01:07:28,280 --> 01:07:30,279
Who dares to do this?

679
01:07:31,320 --> 01:07:32,479
Ulugan.

680
01:07:33,880 --> 01:07:36,079
It was Ulugan's nokers who attacked us.

681
01:07:49,000 --> 01:07:51,159
Do you know?

682
01:07:52,200 --> 01:07:54,479
Even in the swamps that swallow people...

683
01:07:55,240 --> 01:07:58,159
...flowers bloom that attract
a person at first glance.

684
01:07:59,360 --> 01:08:00,559
Allah Allah.

685
01:08:00,920 --> 01:08:03,999
Now, did you think of
flowers in this state, Alaeddin?

686
01:08:04,000 --> 01:08:06,759
No, don't look at me
like that. It's all your fault.

687
01:08:07,200 --> 01:08:11,319
-My fault? -Yes.
-What did I do? -What else can you do?

688
01:08:13,720 --> 01:08:16,439
Even in clothes dirtier than a swamp...

689
01:08:17,560 --> 01:08:19,959
...you shine like those flowers, Hatun.

690
01:08:23,359 --> 01:08:25,158
But I don't like you like this.

691
01:08:26,000 --> 01:08:28,118
Allah Allah, why is that?

692
01:08:28,200 --> 01:08:30,238
I like you! Why don't you like me?!

693
01:08:30,240 --> 01:08:32,639
I don't. I don't like you. What will you do?

694
01:08:32,680 --> 01:08:36,999
-Does a person ever say that to her husband?
-Yes. -The dog Hristo is coming.

695
01:08:40,920 --> 01:08:43,879
-Is Sofia alone?
-Yes.

696
01:08:45,920 --> 01:08:46,959
I asked him.

697
01:08:47,200 --> 01:08:51,599
He is sick. Commander Hristo.
He vomits. He doesn't speak much.

698
01:08:52,840 --> 01:08:54,278
Take him to the healer.

699
01:08:54,720 --> 01:08:57,037
As you order, Commander Hristo.

700
01:09:06,080 --> 01:09:07,999
Well done, Gonca.

701
01:09:11,520 --> 01:09:12,559
Hristo.

702
01:09:13,120 --> 01:09:14,158
Come.

703
01:09:20,520 --> 01:09:22,599
Bala will never stop.

704
01:09:23,960 --> 01:09:26,759
She will look in every hole to find Halime.

705
01:09:28,560 --> 01:09:31,278
I will leave no trails.

706
01:09:31,880 --> 01:09:33,479
Is there such a trail, ma'am?

707
01:09:36,479 --> 01:09:40,078
The Priestess who raised Halime, Lucia...

708
01:09:41,399 --> 01:09:44,238
...lives in a secret monastery. That woman...

709
01:09:46,520 --> 01:09:48,959
...will never speak, Hristo.

710
01:10:00,720 --> 01:10:02,239
Tomorrow, you will go there...

711
01:10:03,160 --> 01:10:07,479
...and kill Priestess Lucia.
-As you order, ma'am.

712
01:10:13,040 --> 01:10:14,079
Bala...

713
01:10:15,280 --> 01:10:18,159
...will never find Halime.

714
01:10:22,160 --> 01:10:23,399
Never.

715
01:10:27,160 --> 01:10:30,039
There is someone who knows who Halime is.

716
01:10:31,400 --> 01:10:35,079
They will kill her to silence her.

717
01:10:35,800 --> 01:10:38,359
No one will stop me...

718
01:10:39,320 --> 01:10:42,319
...from finding my sister, my Halime.

719
01:10:44,320 --> 01:10:47,679
So nokers shouted Ulugan's name...

720
01:10:48,440 --> 01:10:52,999
...while they were attacking, is that so?
-They ambushed us.

721
01:10:53,760 --> 01:10:55,879
Those traitors took their measures.

722
01:10:56,720 --> 01:10:58,959
They suddenly showed up before us.

723
01:10:59,840 --> 01:11:03,919
We fought back, but we retreated
when we lost too many men.

724
01:11:07,960 --> 01:11:10,159
So the one who was with us yesterday...

725
01:11:11,160 --> 01:11:15,719
...killed our nokers without mercy today.

726
01:11:18,400 --> 01:11:20,999
Fate is turning our friends into enemies...

727
01:11:21,560 --> 01:11:25,359
...and enemies into friends.

728
01:11:25,360 --> 01:11:26,959
You did many things though.

729
01:11:27,360 --> 01:11:29,799
You chained Ulugan in front of his nokers.

730
01:11:30,440 --> 01:11:33,519
You came to our tribe and stood against him.

731
01:11:34,560 --> 01:11:35,919
You are right...

732
01:11:54,440 --> 01:11:57,359
Ulugan is blinded by his courage then...

733
01:11:59,120 --> 01:12:00,959
This is really courageous.

734
01:12:02,240 --> 01:12:07,319
He will pay for what he did, of course.
-Of course he will.

735
01:12:07,600 --> 01:12:10,959
Either you will do it or us.

736
01:12:11,640 --> 01:12:14,159
He will get killed by dark steel.

737
01:12:17,320 --> 01:12:18,679
If you'll excuse me...

738
01:12:19,280 --> 01:12:23,159
...I will go to Kayi tribe
and check my casualties.

739
01:12:25,240 --> 01:12:30,519
Bala Hatun, you hosted us well. Thank you.

740
01:12:30,920 --> 01:12:33,719
Kayi always hosts its guests as they deserve.

741
01:12:38,480 --> 01:12:39,759
Shahzade Orhan.

742
01:12:40,880 --> 01:12:42,759
You seem tired.

743
01:12:44,880 --> 01:12:50,319
Yet, it should be you who
looks tired after the defeat.

744
01:12:51,160 --> 01:12:52,639
Right Sargun?

745
01:13:00,760 --> 01:13:02,159
We'll see, Orhan.

746
01:13:03,160 --> 01:13:05,519
We'll see each other often.

747
01:13:05,520 --> 01:13:07,239
Whenever you want.

748
01:13:08,040 --> 01:13:11,359
We can meet anytime you want. Safely.

749
01:13:14,320 --> 01:13:15,719
Remember.

750
01:13:18,320 --> 01:13:20,359
Tomorrow, at Guzelsu...

751
01:13:22,080 --> 01:13:23,639
...we will pay the tax.

752
01:13:35,440 --> 01:13:37,959
There is someone who knows where Halime is.

753
01:13:37,960 --> 01:13:41,399
But Allah knows in which monastery she is.

754
01:13:41,400 --> 01:13:44,719
I'm chasing a chance for my sister, Gonca.

755
01:13:45,200 --> 01:13:48,319
When Hristo leaves, we will
follow him and find that woman.

756
01:13:48,680 --> 01:13:49,719
Alaeddin.

757
01:13:51,400 --> 01:13:55,919
Sofia will do everything to kill
that woman. You know that, right?

758
01:13:58,480 --> 01:14:03,759
I will not let those tyrants who separated
my sister from her family have another joy.

759
01:14:05,480 --> 01:14:07,639
My mother must be worried now.

760
01:14:07,680 --> 01:14:10,959
But when they hear this good
news, they will be very happy.

761
01:14:10,960 --> 01:14:12,679
Yes, they will.

762
01:14:13,680 --> 01:14:17,759
When we make that woman talk
and my sister reunites with her family...

763
01:14:17,800 --> 01:14:20,679
...that joy will last forever, right Gonca?

764
01:14:21,040 --> 01:14:23,639
-Yes.
Come on.

765
01:14:31,000 --> 01:14:32,479
Ulugan Mongolian Camp

766
01:14:57,680 --> 01:15:00,439
Kneel, Altuga!

767
01:15:09,400 --> 01:15:12,319
What do you think you're doing, Esenbike?

768
01:15:15,200 --> 01:15:18,159
I didn't come here to ask questions.

769
01:15:18,840 --> 01:15:21,759
I am here to make you
pay for what you did Ulugan!

770
01:15:28,120 --> 01:15:29,959
My units were ambushed.

771
01:15:30,880 --> 01:15:33,759
My most trusted men were killed.

772
01:15:35,160 --> 01:15:39,239
When they attacked, they
shouted your name, Ulugan.

773
01:15:47,880 --> 01:15:49,599
When the arrival of your units...

774
01:15:50,720 --> 01:15:56,239
...would benefit me the most,
why would I break that power?

775
01:15:57,520 --> 01:16:00,959
How can you believe this, Esenbike?

776
01:16:02,120 --> 01:16:03,959
I surely didn't do this.

777
01:16:07,080 --> 01:16:09,679
While Osman hosted you in his tent...

778
01:16:11,040 --> 01:16:14,119
...he did this behind your back apparently.

779
01:16:22,200 --> 01:16:23,679
You didn't do it.

780
01:16:25,400 --> 01:16:28,839
But Osman planned such a game that...

781
01:16:29,720 --> 01:16:31,519
...when they raided the place...

782
01:16:32,520 --> 01:16:35,479
...they left traces everywhere
that pointed to you.

783
01:16:40,160 --> 01:16:43,879
Traces that you cannot prove otherwise, Ulugan.

784
01:16:57,560 --> 01:17:00,959
I told you that you can't...

785
01:17:01,680 --> 01:17:04,399
...fool Osman with tricks, Esenbike.

786
01:17:05,880 --> 01:17:07,959
He deserved to die.

787
01:17:08,400 --> 01:17:11,239
Let's go kill him.
-No.

788
01:17:14,720 --> 01:17:18,119
Osman is playing a game against us.

789
01:17:20,200 --> 01:17:22,959
We're playing a game against him too.

790
01:17:26,040 --> 01:17:30,879
Osman already accepted paying
taxes. What you said won't happen.

791
01:17:32,920 --> 01:17:34,959
How did he find the gold?

792
01:17:35,200 --> 01:17:38,119
How is he going to pay the tax?

793
01:17:38,680 --> 01:17:41,999
Tomorrow, he'll take the
amount I demanded as the tax...

794
01:17:42,520 --> 01:17:45,519
...from Ayaz Bey and bring it to me.

795
01:17:46,920 --> 01:17:52,519
So he won't have to make
his daughter marry my son.

796
01:17:55,840 --> 01:17:59,799
I mean... He thinks so.

797
01:18:07,880 --> 01:18:10,319
I will ambush Osman...

798
01:18:10,960 --> 01:18:14,119
...and take the gold from him.

799
01:18:14,760 --> 01:18:19,719
So he won't be able to keep his promise.

800
01:18:19,960 --> 01:18:22,039
When he can't pay the taxes

801
01:18:22,440 --> 01:18:25,319
...he will have to make
his daughter marry my son.

802
01:18:28,320 --> 01:18:31,959
That's when the big game begins.

803
01:18:33,280 --> 01:18:37,359
Osman's rebellious head will bow to me.

804
01:18:41,720 --> 01:18:46,959
And then nobody will be able
to stand against Mongolians.

805
01:19:13,440 --> 01:19:19,119
Well... They can break us neither with the
burning dagger they stick into our heart...

806
01:19:19,200 --> 01:19:21,839
...nor with the wounds they open in our chests.

807
01:19:23,680 --> 01:19:26,679
We will cauterize our wounds...

808
01:19:27,560 --> 01:19:30,959
...and always keep walking in the path of Allah.

809
01:19:31,160 --> 01:19:34,439
-God willing, my Bey.
-For sure, my Bey.

810
01:19:35,240 --> 01:19:40,639
But what about the ones who abandoned the
path of Allah and the existing fight of Turks?

811
01:19:40,840 --> 01:19:45,599
Well... The Beys who went to Esenbike...

812
01:19:47,920 --> 01:19:52,679
Although they know Mongolians
slaughtered people in the frontiers.

813
01:19:53,200 --> 01:19:59,999
...how could they believe their
tricks and pledge loyalty to Esenbike?

814
01:20:00,720 --> 01:20:02,479
I don't understand.

815
01:20:02,760 --> 01:20:07,479
Everybody knows what we did to
those who abandoned our cause, my Bey.

816
01:20:09,680 --> 01:20:13,959
As you taught us once, my Bey.

817
01:20:14,320 --> 01:20:20,519
A state is as powerful as the
punishment of the those who betray it.

818
01:20:21,400 --> 01:20:23,999
Nobody should doubt our power.

819
01:20:24,280 --> 01:20:27,639
Any treason against us will be
punished with a sword, my Bey.

820
01:20:30,040 --> 01:20:36,039
Esenbike thinks Beys are the
preys and she herself is the predator.

821
01:20:36,640 --> 01:20:39,319
She laid a trap and drew them on her side.

822
01:20:39,640 --> 01:20:43,199
But we are neither preys nor predators.

823
01:20:44,200 --> 01:20:47,959
We are a high tree under whose shadow...

824
01:20:48,880 --> 01:20:50,879
...they are running.

825
01:20:54,720 --> 01:21:00,239
We want to provide a state with whose
light it will enlighten the whole world!

826
01:21:00,520 --> 01:21:04,879
Definitely, we will punish the treason.

827
01:21:05,000 --> 01:21:12,039
But we should also remove
the curtains before their eyes.

828
01:21:12,240 --> 01:21:15,919
You said right and enlightened our path, my Bey.

829
01:21:16,040 --> 01:21:19,759
Being a state requires us
to get rid of our ambitions...

830
01:21:20,000 --> 01:21:25,879
...and getting united by being patient
even if it feels too heavy for nafs.

831
01:21:25,960 --> 01:21:29,199
It's such an order...

832
01:21:29,400 --> 01:21:32,399
...that the whole world will
be a homeland for Turks.

833
01:21:32,440 --> 01:21:37,719
It's an order that will bring justice
to continents with our swords.

834
01:21:39,320 --> 01:21:42,439
Whoever shows teeth
against us will lose their teeth.

835
01:21:42,480 --> 01:21:45,439
Whoever shows their claws will lose their claws.

836
01:21:45,600 --> 01:21:48,239
We will get united.

837
01:21:48,240 --> 01:21:50,479
For the future of Turks and Islam,

838
01:21:50,520 --> 01:21:54,959
...we'll always keep the
fire of resurrection high.

839
01:21:58,240 --> 01:22:02,199
And we'll stand up
together for the sake of Allah.

840
01:22:02,400 --> 01:22:05,279
-God willing, my Bey.
-God willing, my Bey.

841
01:22:05,920 --> 01:22:11,199
Now we need to pay the tax to Esenbike.

842
01:22:11,920 --> 01:22:13,839
-Ayaz Bey.
-My Bey.

843
01:22:14,400 --> 01:22:16,359
Go to your tribe tomorrow.

844
01:22:16,520 --> 01:22:19,319
Take the carts loaded with chests...

845
01:22:19,840 --> 01:22:23,119
..and come to the border of Karacahisar.

846
01:22:25,400 --> 01:22:28,759
There we will meet Esenbike.

847
01:22:29,560 --> 01:22:31,159
As you order, my Bey.

848
01:22:31,520 --> 01:22:32,879
Now..

849
01:22:33,440 --> 01:22:35,319
Everybody get to work.

850
01:22:35,520 --> 01:22:37,719
Okay my Bey.
Okay my Bey.

851
01:22:42,440 --> 01:22:44,959
-Son.
-My Bey.

852
01:22:48,880 --> 01:22:50,199
My Bey.

853
01:22:50,600 --> 01:22:54,479
It's from Shahzade Alaaddin
Bey. A messenger brought it.

854
01:23:08,600 --> 01:23:10,799
Is it good news, my Bey?

855
01:23:14,520 --> 01:23:17,159
Sofia's dog, Hristo.

856
01:23:18,920 --> 01:23:22,999
The woman who raised Halime...
He's going to visit her tomorrow.

857
01:23:23,880 --> 01:23:26,079
Gonca and Alaaddin...

858
01:23:26,520 --> 01:23:28,519
...are following him.

859
01:24:13,360 --> 01:24:15,199
Meryem.

860
01:24:19,680 --> 01:24:24,039
Bala Hatun, I kept quiet when
I saw you performing prayer.

861
01:24:25,720 --> 01:24:27,679
Ulgen Hatun has sent me.

862
01:24:34,760 --> 01:24:36,759
Thank you, girl.

863
01:24:42,520 --> 01:24:44,639
It looks beautiful.

864
01:24:45,240 --> 01:24:48,599
We've got one step closer to Halime, Meryem.

865
01:25:00,800 --> 01:25:02,799
Is it good?

866
01:25:10,120 --> 01:25:13,759
It's hot but it smells very good.

867
01:25:13,880 --> 01:25:18,599
It smells good because you touched it.

868
01:25:21,440 --> 01:25:23,199
Come here, girl.

869
01:25:24,040 --> 01:25:26,599
Wait, it's too hot.

870
01:25:39,440 --> 01:25:42,559
Come on, come on.

871
01:25:44,240 --> 01:25:45,879
I'm full.

872
01:25:46,280 --> 01:25:49,479
You can't go before it's finished, Halime. Come.

873
01:25:49,880 --> 01:25:55,559
Halime, wait. My girl... Halime!

874
01:25:56,040 --> 01:25:58,879
You have to finish the soup, Halime.

875
01:25:59,640 --> 01:26:01,319
Come here.

876
01:26:01,720 --> 01:26:05,799
Halime, you have to finish the soup. My girl!

877
01:26:06,360 --> 01:26:09,759
Don't make me run! Well..

878
01:26:10,960 --> 01:26:12,719
I got you.

879
01:26:12,800 --> 01:26:14,919
I'll eat if you turn me.

880
01:26:15,120 --> 01:26:16,919
You want to play, huh?

881
01:26:17,200 --> 01:26:19,439
Come here.

882
01:26:20,600 --> 01:26:21,599
My Halime...

883
01:26:35,640 --> 01:26:37,479
My beautiful, daughter.

884
01:26:37,760 --> 01:26:40,119
You want to play, huh?

885
01:26:40,320 --> 01:26:42,359
You want o play?

886
01:26:45,640 --> 01:26:47,719
My beautiful girl.

887
01:26:50,040 --> 01:26:51,679
Meryem.

888
01:26:54,640 --> 01:26:56,599
Meryem, are you alright?

889
01:26:57,760 --> 01:26:59,159
Meryem.

890
01:26:59,920 --> 01:27:05,159
Meryem, are you alright? Do you hear me? Meryem?

891
01:27:06,120 --> 01:27:07,799
Mother.

892
01:27:13,200 --> 01:27:14,679
My girl.

893
01:27:18,480 --> 01:27:22,079
My girl. My girl, Meryem.

894
01:27:22,240 --> 01:27:25,439
Meryem, Meryem.

895
01:27:25,640 --> 01:27:28,519
My Allah... Oh..

896
01:27:31,360 --> 01:27:35,799
Meryem! My girl... Meryem

897
01:27:36,960 --> 01:27:40,239
My girl, do you hear me? Are you alright?

898
01:27:40,840 --> 01:27:42,999
I'm fine. I'm fine.

899
01:27:46,680 --> 01:27:48,719
I was dreaming.

900
01:27:52,200 --> 01:27:54,119
I saw my mother.

901
01:27:57,280 --> 01:28:01,039
You must have got exhausted.

902
01:28:02,040 --> 01:28:05,159
Don't go anywhere today. Rest in your tent.

903
01:28:06,960 --> 01:28:09,239
Come on, my girl.

904
01:28:12,200 --> 01:28:15,199
Mother, is there something wrong?

905
01:28:15,280 --> 01:28:17,039
It's alright, my girl.

906
01:28:17,480 --> 01:28:19,919
Meryem is like a little sick.

907
01:28:23,160 --> 01:28:27,879
-Ulgen, take care of Meryem.
-Alright. Come here.

908
01:28:29,240 --> 01:28:31,399
Don't worry, Bala.

909
01:28:35,680 --> 01:28:38,439
-I should finish the preparations.
-Mother.

910
01:28:39,840 --> 01:28:43,799
I'll go with you. I can help you in the temple.

911
01:28:44,520 --> 01:28:47,919
No, my girl. You're pregnant. You stay.
-Mother.

912
01:28:48,440 --> 01:28:51,999
I know them well. I speak their language.

913
01:28:52,440 --> 01:28:56,759
-Let me go with you.
-Fine.

914
01:28:57,440 --> 01:28:59,159
You can.

915
01:28:59,400 --> 01:29:02,799
Let's go find Priestess Lucia.
-Alright.

916
01:29:03,160 --> 01:29:05,279
Let's finish the preparations.

917
01:29:07,040 --> 01:29:08,919
Lucia?

918
01:29:29,640 --> 01:29:32,159
Oh my tribe...

919
01:29:34,440 --> 01:29:40,039
Oh... Oh..

920
01:29:46,040 --> 01:29:48,519
My cause.

921
01:29:51,800 --> 01:29:54,039
My issue.

922
01:29:56,240 --> 01:29:59,599
Jackals raiding my dreams.

923
01:30:04,640 --> 01:30:10,199
They built obstacles on my ideal.

924
01:30:22,840 --> 01:30:23,999
Help my, my Allah.

925
01:30:26,920 --> 01:30:32,079
Help me, my Allah.
Help me, my Allah.

926
01:30:33,280 --> 01:30:36,799
O The Most Merciful of the merciful.

927
01:30:38,680 --> 01:30:41,679
Oh Almighty Allah..

928
01:30:42,840 --> 01:30:44,639
I'm here for Your help.

929
01:30:45,520 --> 01:30:48,239
I'm here for Your help, my Allah.

930
01:30:48,360 --> 01:30:50,879
I bow to You, my Allah.

931
01:30:52,040 --> 01:30:55,999
I'd gladly sacrifice my head for You, my Allah.

932
01:30:57,120 --> 01:30:59,239
I see Your Grace.

933
01:31:02,480 --> 01:31:04,759
I see Your help, my Allah.

934
01:31:09,000 --> 01:31:11,199
We are just a few, my Allah.

935
01:31:12,320 --> 01:31:14,039
They are too many.

936
01:31:14,760 --> 01:31:16,519
For coins.

937
01:31:17,960 --> 01:31:19,319
For fame.

938
01:31:19,960 --> 01:31:21,919
For glory.

939
01:31:23,360 --> 01:31:27,559
The number of those abandoning
Your path has increased, my Allah.

940
01:31:28,080 --> 01:31:32,559
The number of those holding Your
divine rope has decreased, my Allah.

941
01:31:35,240 --> 01:31:37,039
We are just a few.

942
01:31:39,160 --> 01:31:40,999
Only a few.

943
01:31:41,400 --> 01:31:43,399
We're helpless.

944
01:31:45,600 --> 01:31:47,159
Allah.

945
01:31:48,720 --> 01:31:49,559
O Creator!

946
01:31:52,080 --> 01:31:53,839
For the sake of...

947
01:31:54,560 --> 01:31:59,919
...our Prophet, peace be upon you, who said
that the companions of the poor...

948
01:32:00,440 --> 01:32:02,399
...are Allah and His messenger.

949
01:32:05,440 --> 01:32:07,239
Let this poor man..

950
01:32:08,360 --> 01:32:10,719
...be Your companion.

951
01:32:11,800 --> 01:32:14,279
Help me make my few many.

952
01:32:15,280 --> 01:32:18,079
Help me make up my shortage, my Allah.

953
01:32:19,720 --> 01:32:21,159
Don't leave me...

954
01:32:22,240 --> 01:32:25,119
...to heathens, my Allah.

955
01:32:27,680 --> 01:32:31,039
My Allah, give me strength.

956
01:32:33,200 --> 01:32:35,519
Give me power.

957
01:32:36,240 --> 01:32:38,199
During this tough fight.

958
01:32:38,840 --> 01:32:43,239
...make me and those
supporting me victorious, my Allah.

959
01:32:44,160 --> 01:32:48,679
My Allah, let me take back my tribe...

960
01:32:49,600 --> 01:32:52,559
...and protect my state.

961
01:32:53,440 --> 01:33:01,719
Help me spread Your glorious
Name all around the world, my Allah.

962
01:33:33,200 --> 01:33:35,159
We're ready to move, my Bey.

963
01:33:35,560 --> 01:33:38,519
God willing, we will have a
double victory today, my Bey.

964
01:33:39,200 --> 01:33:40,959
God willing, God willing.

965
01:33:41,360 --> 01:33:44,559
Those who weaving the webs of evil will see...

966
01:33:45,200 --> 01:33:47,679
Even if they bend the wing of Turks,

967
01:33:47,960 --> 01:33:50,119
...they can never break it.

968
01:33:52,840 --> 01:33:54,439
Here we go.

969
01:34:22,520 --> 01:34:24,839
Osman has set out, Ulugan.

970
01:34:25,840 --> 01:34:27,919
Finally.

971
01:34:28,400 --> 01:34:31,399
The gold he desires so much...

972
01:34:31,960 --> 01:34:34,999
..will be strained with Osman's filthy blood.

973
01:34:38,320 --> 01:34:40,319
Are you going to kill him, Ulugan?

974
01:34:41,000 --> 01:34:42,839
What about Esenbike?

975
01:34:43,000 --> 01:34:44,919
-She wants peace...
-Peace...

976
01:34:48,440 --> 01:34:52,839
...is provided when the
strong one destroys the enemy.

977
01:34:53,840 --> 01:34:58,719
Today, Osman's lifeless head...

978
01:35:00,080 --> 01:35:02,839
...is going to kiss under my feet.

979
01:35:10,520 --> 01:35:12,639
Am I going crazy?

980
01:35:13,800 --> 01:35:16,519
Why is this happening to me?

981
01:35:19,800 --> 01:35:20,999
Meryem.

982
01:35:21,280 --> 01:35:22,399
Are you alright?

983
01:35:22,560 --> 01:35:25,839
-I'm fine, Ulgen Hatun.
-Don't stand up. Don't.

984
01:35:26,080 --> 01:35:28,919
I promised Bala. You
have to rest until she's back.

985
01:35:29,720 --> 01:35:31,319
But I'm fine.

986
01:35:31,440 --> 01:35:35,519
If you insist, I'll send Ghazi here.
He'll destroy you with his nagging.

987
01:35:36,200 --> 01:35:39,759
-Alright. I won't stand up.
-Okay. Lie down.

988
01:35:39,840 --> 01:35:42,919
-Lie down there. Have a good rest.
-I won't stand up.

989
01:35:43,040 --> 01:35:44,879
You're comfortable?

990
01:35:45,120 --> 01:35:47,599
Have a good rest. I'll be back.

991
01:35:48,880 --> 01:35:50,799
Ulgen Hatun.

992
01:35:52,200 --> 01:35:55,559
Bala Hatun mentioned a priestess.

993
01:35:57,960 --> 01:36:00,759
-Do you know who she is?
-Yes.

994
01:36:01,640 --> 01:36:03,999
The priestess who raised Halime.

995
01:36:05,680 --> 01:36:08,839
Lu... Lucia or..

996
01:36:09,000 --> 01:36:11,039
A foreigner name like that.

997
01:36:15,160 --> 01:36:17,599
Sitting up again? Lie down!

998
01:36:23,520 --> 01:36:25,239
I'll be back.

999
01:36:32,440 --> 01:36:36,119
Lucia raised me not Halime.

1000
01:36:36,960 --> 01:36:38,839
She's my aunt's only confidant.

1001
01:36:40,720 --> 01:36:43,079
I have to let my aunt know.

1002
01:36:54,080 --> 01:36:56,039
But if she goes there

1003
01:36:57,320 --> 01:36:59,119
...Bala Hatun will be there.

1004
01:37:00,560 --> 01:37:02,719
They'll kill each other.

1005
01:37:06,200 --> 01:37:09,559
Yes, Holofira insisted on coming with us.

1006
01:37:09,600 --> 01:37:11,519
I wouldn't have let her, but...

1007
01:37:11,640 --> 01:37:13,999
I'll be alright with you, mother. Don't worry.

1008
01:37:14,040 --> 01:37:17,119
I can help you a lot in the monastery.
-That's right.

1009
01:37:17,360 --> 01:37:21,719
But we don't know which monastery it is.

1010
01:37:27,680 --> 01:37:29,959
Someone's coming. Come on.

1011
01:37:38,200 --> 01:37:41,599
Soldiers, we won't stop until we reach Odios!

1012
01:37:41,680 --> 01:37:44,999
Even I can't save you
from Sofia this time! Let's go!

1013
01:37:47,480 --> 01:37:52,039
Photinodios. I know that place.

1014
01:37:57,640 --> 01:37:59,159
Let's go.

1015
01:38:00,960 --> 01:38:03,279
We have to reach there before them.

1016
01:38:03,320 --> 01:38:06,719
We should make her speak
before those dogs kill her.

1017
01:38:07,080 --> 01:38:10,519
-Holofira, do you know a shortcut? -I do.

1018
01:38:10,760 --> 01:38:14,439
But not far away from the way Hristo is using.

1019
01:38:16,040 --> 01:38:18,879
Alps, you follow Hristo.

1020
01:38:19,080 --> 01:38:22,559
-Stop them from reaching the monastery.
-As you order, Bala Hatun.

1021
01:38:23,320 --> 01:38:26,359
We should reach there
quickly through the shortcut.

1022
01:38:26,480 --> 01:38:27,479
Let's go.

1023
01:38:27,520 --> 01:38:29,799
-Let's go.
-Come on, come on.

1024
01:38:33,440 --> 01:38:35,519
Alaca. Come on, my girl.

1025
01:39:00,680 --> 01:39:02,159
Go, Osman.

1026
01:39:03,000 --> 01:39:04,319
I will spill your blood...

1027
01:39:04,960 --> 01:39:09,039
...into the hearts of all
the mountains of this world.

1028
01:39:09,680 --> 01:39:13,879
Ulugan, why don't we take his
life now? What are we waiting for?

1029
01:39:13,920 --> 01:39:15,039
Wait.

1030
01:39:15,720 --> 01:39:17,959
Let's see the gold first...

1031
01:39:20,200 --> 01:39:23,359
So we will take both his life and his wealth.

1032
01:39:26,800 --> 01:39:28,959
After taking Osman's life...

1033
01:39:28,960 --> 01:39:33,439
...those who will want to take his
revenge must also be left helpless.

1034
01:39:35,440 --> 01:39:39,159
Let's go. Let's go without being noticed.

1035
01:39:44,720 --> 01:39:45,999
My Mother Sultan.

1036
01:39:47,400 --> 01:39:49,839
I said she was a shepherd's daughter, but...

1037
01:39:50,560 --> 01:39:52,759
...I didn't expect her to be like this.

1038
01:39:53,880 --> 01:39:56,359
-Fatma Hatun...
She is very beautiful.

1039
01:39:57,320 --> 01:40:02,039
Very smart, very merciful. -Yes.

1040
01:40:04,880 --> 01:40:09,439
I want this marriage as much as you do now.

1041
01:40:10,240 --> 01:40:15,159
My only fear is that Osman Bey won't agree.

1042
01:40:21,520 --> 01:40:23,119
Until now..

1043
01:40:24,720 --> 01:40:27,799
...what have we wanted that
we haven't taken, my lion?

1044
01:40:30,560 --> 01:40:36,079
I will leave Osman Bey no
choice but to give his daughter.

1045
01:40:39,320 --> 01:40:43,719
Fatma will eventually become your bride.

1046
01:40:49,680 --> 01:40:52,719
This woman will use us
and kill us. What will we do?

1047
01:40:53,560 --> 01:40:54,959
It's not that easy, Begum.

1048
01:40:56,000 --> 01:40:58,559
I suffered heavily to get here.

1049
01:40:58,760 --> 01:41:01,759
I won't give up my position, you, or my life.

1050
01:41:01,760 --> 01:41:03,359
What's your plan?

1051
01:41:04,440 --> 01:41:06,279
We will play the biggest game.

1052
01:41:10,000 --> 01:41:11,799
We must get there before Hristo.

1053
01:41:11,800 --> 01:41:15,639
If that woman speaks, we
will find Halime soon. Alaeddin!

1054
01:41:15,640 --> 01:41:17,877
We will make it,
mother, we will, come on!

1055
01:41:17,889 --> 01:41:18,639
Soon...

1056
01:41:18,640 --> 01:41:22,879
I am coming my Halime! We will come,
my daughter, we will meet. Let's go!

1057
01:41:50,640 --> 01:41:52,279
Now we will change the path.

1058
01:41:52,280 --> 01:41:54,679
We will go this way to get rid of them.

1059
01:41:54,680 --> 01:41:56,599
-As you order my Bey.
-Alps!

1060
01:41:56,920 --> 01:42:00,159
You will come after us and
remove the shoeprints. Come on!

1061
01:42:26,800 --> 01:42:30,639
Osman is playing games again.

1062
01:42:30,720 --> 01:42:33,159
He never lets go of his suspicion.

1063
01:42:33,480 --> 01:42:35,319
Let him do his best.

1064
01:42:35,960 --> 01:42:37,999
All his efforts are in vain.

1065
01:42:38,720 --> 01:42:40,559
Let's surround him.

1066
01:42:54,960 --> 01:42:57,239
My Bey, Ayaz Bey is coming.

1067
01:43:15,800 --> 01:43:17,039
Peace be upon you.

1068
01:43:17,160 --> 01:43:18,639
Peace be upon you, too.

1069
01:43:18,640 --> 01:43:20,879
All the gold is here, my Bey.

1070
01:43:21,920 --> 01:43:25,599
You stood by us in this
difficult time, Ayaz Bey.

1071
01:43:25,600 --> 01:43:29,039
Thank you, give us your pardon.
-It's yours, my Bey.

1072
01:43:29,600 --> 01:43:30,759
Osman

1073
01:43:35,120 --> 01:43:37,359
You have to ask me first!

1074
01:43:38,800 --> 01:43:42,799
But you will pay for it with your life.

1075
01:43:43,600 --> 01:43:48,759
I had a dream. Your lineage will
end and your land will be ruined.

1076
01:43:48,760 --> 01:43:52,999
Just because a jackal had a dream, it
doesn't mean the wolves will go extinct.

1077
01:43:53,000 --> 01:43:57,199
There were many like you in
these lands before. Don't worry.

1078
01:43:57,400 --> 01:44:00,519
My steel sword will bring your death.

1079
01:44:00,520 --> 01:44:03,239
Then let's settle our account.

1080
01:44:08,800 --> 01:44:09,839
Ayaz.

1081
01:44:10,560 --> 01:44:13,439
Take the chests.
-As you order, my Bey.

1082
01:44:16,240 --> 01:44:17,359
Attack!

1083
01:44:35,880 --> 01:44:39,279
May Lord Jesus protect you. Priestess Lucia.

1084
01:44:39,320 --> 01:44:40,799
We came to see her.

1085
01:44:41,120 --> 01:44:43,359
We weren't expecting any guests today.

1086
01:44:46,040 --> 01:44:48,839
It was especially requested to be kept secret.

1087
01:44:53,160 --> 01:44:58,279
We came all the way from the Monastery of
Saint John in Constantinople just for this.

1088
01:44:59,480 --> 01:45:02,559
So, Saint John. Who sent you from there?

1089
01:45:12,320 --> 01:45:13,959
Priest Hodegon.

1090
01:45:14,440 --> 01:45:17,519
He told us to see Priestess Lucia.

1091
01:45:29,360 --> 01:45:31,959
We have important things to tell her.

1092
01:45:32,360 --> 01:45:34,159
Forgive us, ma'am.

1093
01:45:34,640 --> 01:45:35,679
Here.

1094
01:46:40,640 --> 01:46:43,959
They killed Marcus and took his place.

1095
01:46:44,080 --> 01:46:48,359
The man who brought the goods
said he was sick. They left at night.

1096
01:46:58,120 --> 01:46:59,519
Idiots!

1097
01:47:01,520 --> 01:47:03,599
Did you believe this?

1098
01:47:07,040 --> 01:47:10,759
If they left, they must have
learned what they wanted.

1099
01:47:15,560 --> 01:47:16,919
Damn it.

1100
01:47:21,200 --> 01:47:23,039
They are after Hristo.

1101
01:47:25,400 --> 01:47:27,399
-We're leaving.
-As you order.

1102
01:47:37,640 --> 01:47:40,399
Ulugan... I will do terrible things to you...

1103
01:47:40,960 --> 01:47:44,719
Don't tire yourself. You
have a few breaths left.

1104
01:47:51,440 --> 01:47:54,679
Nokers! Protect Ulugan, come on!

1105
01:47:59,640 --> 01:48:02,319
Ulugan! You can't fight
in this condition. Get up!

1106
01:48:02,320 --> 01:48:06,279
-Give me my sword!
-Leave, Ulugan!

1107
01:48:06,280 --> 01:48:08,319
-I'll keep them here, go!
-My Bey!

1108
01:48:21,800 --> 01:48:25,839
Ulugan, come on! Nokers!
Protect Ulugan, come on!

1109
01:48:29,920 --> 01:48:30,959
My Bey!

1110
01:48:33,040 --> 01:48:34,999
The dog Ulugan is running away!

1111
01:48:39,600 --> 01:48:40,679
Brother.

1112
01:48:42,720 --> 01:48:47,479
-Come, don't betray your people while dying.
-Altuga.

1113
01:48:49,040 --> 01:48:51,399
You're still trying to play games.

1114
01:48:53,040 --> 01:48:56,679
But now the game is
over. This is the battlefield.

1115
01:48:56,800 --> 01:48:58,599
Now I will teach you this.

1116
01:49:00,040 --> 01:49:01,399
You will teach me, huh?

1117
01:49:03,320 --> 01:49:04,519
You will teach me.

1118
01:49:23,760 --> 01:49:25,319
Ulugan!

1119
01:49:29,960 --> 01:49:33,519
Today, even these beech trees
you trust so much will not protect you

1120
01:49:33,880 --> 01:49:34,959
Nokers!

1121
01:49:35,720 --> 01:49:37,399
Come on! Keep them there!

1122
01:49:40,000 --> 01:49:44,119
Where are you going?

1123
01:49:53,080 --> 01:49:55,999
Priestess Lucia is waiting for you, come in.

1124
01:50:02,480 --> 01:50:04,239
Soldiers, you stay here.

1125
01:50:38,040 --> 01:50:39,919
Hurry, Alps

1126
01:50:42,840 --> 01:50:45,719
Now this is the end of
the way for you all, infidels!

1127
01:50:46,040 --> 01:50:47,239
Come!

1128
01:51:00,720 --> 01:51:03,399
Our swords will be watered with blood!

1129
01:51:31,200 --> 01:51:32,519
Give up already.

1130
01:51:34,160 --> 01:51:35,999
You have no moves left to make!

1131
01:51:37,720 --> 01:51:39,959
Now...

1132
01:51:40,440 --> 01:51:42,919
...it is time for you to go to Ucmag.

1133
01:51:42,920 --> 01:51:45,319
I can go to Ucmag but...

1134
01:51:45,800 --> 01:51:46,839
..you..

1135
01:51:47,640 --> 01:51:48,679
..you..

1136
01:51:49,160 --> 01:51:51,839
...will face Erlik Khan's furor, brother.

1137
01:51:54,560 --> 01:51:55,599
Come on!

1138
01:52:08,400 --> 01:52:09,879
Traitor brother...

1139
01:52:11,720 --> 01:52:14,119
Kill me, brother.

1140
01:52:14,120 --> 01:52:18,559
Kill me and send me to our mother Meral Hatun.

1141
01:52:22,720 --> 01:52:25,199
I will tell her that..

1142
01:52:26,040 --> 01:52:29,679
...her own son, my brother
Cerkutay sent me there.

1143
01:52:31,120 --> 01:52:32,159
Kill me.

1144
01:52:32,960 --> 01:52:35,919
Don't show me mercy, brother! Kill me!

1145
01:52:39,200 --> 01:52:43,319
You are weak, brother.

1146
01:52:46,000 --> 01:52:47,479
You are still weak.

1147
01:53:26,920 --> 01:53:28,079
Alps!

1148
01:53:28,080 --> 01:53:31,599
Gather here!

1149
01:53:34,000 --> 01:53:35,319
Cerkutay Bey.

1150
01:53:35,720 --> 01:53:37,439
Brother... what happened?

1151
01:53:39,720 --> 01:53:40,959
I couldn't kill him.

1152
01:53:42,400 --> 01:53:43,799
I couldn't..

1153
01:53:45,200 --> 01:53:49,039
I could not move after he
said my mother's name...

1154
01:53:50,720 --> 01:53:51,959
Cerkutay Bey.

1155
01:53:52,800 --> 01:53:54,119
Don't worry.

1156
01:53:54,720 --> 01:53:57,319
What you are going to do is not easy.

1157
01:53:59,680 --> 01:54:00,719
Alps.

1158
01:54:00,760 --> 01:54:03,279
Is everyone alright? -We are alright my Bey.

1159
01:54:03,280 --> 01:54:07,439
We are, my Shahzade.
-Come on then.

1160
01:54:07,720 --> 01:54:09,399
We will go to my father.

1161
01:54:30,080 --> 01:54:32,359
Stop there... Stop there...

1162
01:54:32,800 --> 01:54:37,719
Many had the chance of
suffering from my slap before you.

1163
01:54:39,880 --> 01:54:41,479
Now it's your turn.

1164
01:54:42,400 --> 01:54:44,239
I won't fall easily.

1165
01:54:44,360 --> 01:54:47,639
You cannot defeat me, Osman.
-You will fall!

1166
01:54:48,760 --> 01:54:50,559
You will fall in such a way that...

1167
01:54:51,520 --> 01:54:54,599
My name is Osman Bey! I came to this world...

1168
01:54:54,920 --> 01:54:58,199
...to make those like you
pay for what you have done!

1169
01:54:59,480 --> 01:55:05,639
I came to this world to stamp the mark of
justice that will never fade on your forehead!

1170
01:55:05,640 --> 01:55:07,679
You will fail.

1171
01:55:15,400 --> 01:55:16,759
Is that so?

1172
01:55:17,440 --> 01:55:18,759
Is that so?

1173
01:55:24,080 --> 01:55:25,239
Almighty Allah...

1174
01:55:26,120 --> 01:55:29,159
...sent me here so I could
fight against those like you.

1175
01:55:29,840 --> 01:55:31,839
But I swear to Allah...

1176
01:55:32,360 --> 01:55:35,079
...until I kill you and others like you...

1177
01:55:36,520 --> 01:55:38,479
...I will never stop.

1178
01:56:15,440 --> 01:56:19,039
Now the era of Ulugan is over.

1179
01:56:52,760 --> 01:56:55,599
I have never seen you before. Who are you?

1180
01:56:56,160 --> 01:56:57,999
You actually know me.

1181
01:57:03,200 --> 01:57:06,919
For God's sake, what is happening?
-There is nothing to be scared of.

1182
01:57:06,920 --> 01:57:09,879
I am Osman Bey's Hatun, Bala Hatun.

1183
01:57:16,240 --> 01:57:17,559
You are not surprised.

1184
01:57:19,640 --> 01:57:21,479
You were waiting for me then.

1185
01:57:21,560 --> 01:57:23,439
Where is my daughter?

1186
01:57:24,280 --> 01:57:26,879
I knew this sin would not let me go.

1187
01:57:27,040 --> 01:57:29,999
I've been waiting for you
for ten years, Bala Hatun.

1188
01:57:30,560 --> 01:57:34,079
Priestess Lucia, God will never forgive you.

1189
01:57:34,320 --> 01:57:36,839
You separated a mother and a child.

1190
01:57:37,080 --> 01:57:39,599
You committed the greatest sin!

1191
01:57:39,840 --> 01:57:42,039
Now is not the time to confess the sins!

1192
01:57:42,360 --> 01:57:43,959
Tell me where my daughter is.

1193
01:57:44,920 --> 01:57:46,239
I can't tell you that...

1194
01:57:46,320 --> 01:57:47,559
Sofia won't let me live.

1195
01:57:47,560 --> 01:57:48,999
You will die anyway!

1196
01:57:49,400 --> 01:57:51,159
I am here to save you.

1197
01:57:52,160 --> 01:57:55,119
Sofia sent Hristo to have you killed.

1198
01:58:13,200 --> 01:58:14,879
I will see Priestess Lucia.

1199
01:58:14,920 --> 01:58:16,399
I brought news from Sofia.

1200
01:58:20,880 --> 01:58:22,039
They are already here.

1201
01:58:40,440 --> 01:58:41,839
Sofia exposed her secret.

1202
01:58:41,840 --> 01:58:45,599
Now she wants to kill
everyone who knows her secret.

1203
01:58:45,600 --> 01:58:46,799
It's your turn.

1204
01:58:46,800 --> 01:58:48,399
Speak before your death comes.

1205
01:58:49,640 --> 01:58:53,319
Tell us where Halime is. We don't have time.
-I don't know.

1206
01:58:53,680 --> 01:58:57,719
I am telling you that Sofia will kill
everyone who knows her secret!

1207
01:58:57,960 --> 01:58:59,039
You decide.

1208
01:59:02,960 --> 01:59:08,079
Tell him that I left to go to the village
and that he should wait for a while.

1209
01:59:10,560 --> 01:59:12,239
She..

1210
01:59:16,120 --> 01:59:17,279
Just like you...

1211
01:59:19,120 --> 01:59:21,519
...she is fearless and beautiful.

1212
01:59:31,920 --> 01:59:33,119
Where is she now?

1213
01:59:36,800 --> 01:59:38,919
She raised her like her own daughter.

1214
01:59:39,960 --> 01:59:41,519
She never left her side.

1215
01:59:42,080 --> 01:59:43,839
She loves her like her mother...

1216
01:59:44,480 --> 01:59:45,839
Snake!

1217
01:59:47,480 --> 01:59:49,399
Snake!

1218
01:59:51,280 --> 01:59:53,877
When will she come
back from the village?

1219
01:59:53,889 --> 01:59:54,759
I don't know.

1220
01:59:55,360 --> 01:59:57,599
Sofia is coming!
Sofia is coming!

1221
02:00:00,680 --> 02:00:02,479
Damn it!

1222
02:00:02,640 --> 02:00:04,279
Why did that woman come here?

1223
02:00:05,600 --> 02:00:07,319
Let's go and find my mother.

1224
02:00:07,320 --> 02:00:10,359
We have to leave this place immediately. Come

1225
02:00:12,960 --> 02:00:16,079
Tell me, where is my Halime?
Where does she keep her?

1226
02:00:16,560 --> 02:00:17,799
She is not Halime.

1227
02:00:22,160 --> 02:00:23,199
Alaeddin.

1228
02:00:24,560 --> 02:00:27,959
Mother, Sofia found it out. She
is coming here with her soldiers.

1229
02:00:28,280 --> 02:00:30,199
We need to leave now.

1230
02:00:31,360 --> 02:00:32,999
Sofia is coming for you.

1231
02:00:33,000 --> 02:00:35,199
You will come with me if you want to live.

1232
02:00:35,200 --> 02:00:36,839
Which way should we go? Tell us!

1233
02:00:38,120 --> 02:00:41,319
Are there any other exits besides the main gate?

1234
02:00:44,920 --> 02:00:46,079
Bala is here!

1235
02:00:46,280 --> 02:00:48,879
Close all the gates! Hurry!

1236
02:00:49,840 --> 02:00:52,439
What are you saying, Sofia?

1237
02:00:53,040 --> 02:00:54,279
Idiot!

1238
02:00:54,440 --> 02:00:56,599
While you are waiting here...

1239
02:00:56,760 --> 02:00:59,639
...Bala is making Lucia speak inside!

1240
02:01:01,680 --> 02:01:02,719
Come on!

1241
02:01:20,880 --> 02:01:23,969
Around Guzelsu

1242
02:01:24,240 --> 02:01:27,839
Last night, he tricked us.

1243
02:01:29,120 --> 02:01:32,439
I want to cut off Osman's
head when he comes, but...

1244
02:01:32,600 --> 02:01:34,559
Don't worry, son.

1245
02:01:35,640 --> 02:01:37,799
It will be as we wish.

1246
02:01:38,920 --> 02:01:42,479
When Ulugan takes the gold from Ayaz,

1247
02:01:43,240 --> 02:01:48,359
...Osman will get his tail between his
legs and make his daughter marry you.

1248
02:01:52,880 --> 02:01:56,239
Esenbike Hatun, Osman's coming.

1249
02:02:02,520 --> 02:02:05,079
What's the cart behind him?

1250
02:02:05,640 --> 02:02:11,039
-Did he... Did he get rid of
Ulugan and bring the tax, mother?

1251
02:02:16,600 --> 02:02:19,719
-Osman Bey.
-As we agreed.

1252
02:02:20,880 --> 02:02:23,479
I've brought the tax.

1253
02:02:26,120 --> 02:02:29,999
What? Weren't you expecting this?

1254
02:02:30,320 --> 02:02:33,959
-Ha, Esenbike Hatun.
-Of course, I was.

1255
02:02:36,400 --> 02:02:40,399
Let me see the gold which
is the price of our peace.

1256
02:02:42,480 --> 02:02:44,439
Let's see then.

1257
02:03:09,160 --> 02:03:11,159
Open it.

1258
02:03:31,720 --> 02:03:34,159
What does this mean, Osman Bey?

1259
02:03:34,840 --> 02:03:36,799
Are you playing a trick?

1260
02:03:37,520 --> 02:03:40,159
Do you have a death wish?

1261
02:03:45,200 --> 02:03:47,719
Kanyumaz! Samil!

1262
02:03:54,000 --> 02:03:55,879
Bring.

1263
02:04:06,200 --> 02:04:07,719
Ulugan.

1264
02:04:08,000 --> 02:04:09,719
Yes, Ulugan.

1265
02:04:10,560 --> 02:04:12,039
Ulugan.

1266
02:04:14,920 --> 02:04:20,679
I'm thirsty for the life of your
rebellious commander Ulugan.

1267
02:04:45,040 --> 02:04:48,239
This door. But it hasn't been used for long.

1268
02:04:48,520 --> 02:04:50,599
Come on.

1269
02:04:58,560 --> 02:05:01,359
I'll look after you until I find Halime.

1270
02:05:01,600 --> 02:05:03,199
Her name isn't Halime.

1271
02:05:03,640 --> 02:05:07,959
-She doesn't remember her name, you or anything.
-What's her name?

1272
02:05:09,920 --> 02:05:11,959
Bala!

1273
02:05:34,720 --> 02:05:37,839
Her name is Poena.

1274
02:06:11,840 --> 02:06:16,239
What I've brought for you isn't the gold.

1275
02:06:19,600 --> 02:06:23,599
The tax I pay you is the head...

1276
02:06:24,480 --> 02:06:27,559
...of the dog called
Ulugan you were looking for.

1277
02:06:30,120 --> 02:06:31,559
Stop.

1278
02:06:32,000 --> 02:06:33,519
Nokers!

1279
02:06:45,400 --> 02:06:48,679
That sword will never touch Ulugan!

1280
02:06:49,600 --> 02:06:51,919
Otherwise you can't survive here.

1281
02:06:54,520 --> 02:06:56,039
Beys!

1282
02:07:03,880 --> 02:07:06,079
Come here.

1283
02:07:10,520 --> 02:07:12,319
Come and see.

1284
02:07:12,640 --> 02:07:14,359
See this hatun..

1285
02:07:14,600 --> 02:07:21,239
...who was supposed to protect our
tribe and people from Ulugan's tyranny.

1286
02:07:29,200 --> 02:07:30,959
Just wait.

1287
02:07:31,200 --> 02:07:33,239
Wait for a while.

1288
02:07:33,400 --> 02:07:35,959
I won't kill you so easily.

1289
02:07:38,320 --> 02:07:40,279
Are you afraid, Osman?

1290
02:07:41,200 --> 02:07:45,719
Are you afraid of the powerful Mongolian army...

1291
02:07:45,960 --> 02:07:49,039
...who would come for you if you killed me?

1292
02:07:51,880 --> 02:07:55,239
You're right.

1293
02:07:55,760 --> 02:07:58,559
Yes... But still

1294
02:08:00,200 --> 02:08:03,439
...we will come for you.

1295
02:08:04,520 --> 02:08:07,199
Where are you going, Ulugan?

1296
02:08:10,000 --> 02:08:12,999
-Oh...
Just wait.

1297
02:08:16,200 --> 02:08:19,239
We have a matter to settle.

1298
02:08:35,000 --> 02:08:37,479
You got tricked by the wolf?

1299
02:08:45,360 --> 02:08:48,759
While you thought I was seeking the gold,

1300
02:08:55,560 --> 02:08:57,839
...I was seeking you.

1301
02:08:58,360 --> 02:09:00,199
Osman.

1302
02:09:00,400 --> 02:09:02,599
Yes, Osman.

1303
02:09:03,080 --> 02:09:04,959
Of course, Osman.

1304
02:09:05,800 --> 02:09:09,999
Did you think I didn't notice the
game you and Esenbike were playing?

1305
02:09:10,600 --> 02:09:15,119
I'm the ruler of these lands.
These lands belong to me.

1306
02:09:15,920 --> 02:09:20,439
I know even the worms inside
the throat of the bird flying here.

1307
02:09:31,080 --> 02:09:33,239
Just wait.

1308
02:09:33,960 --> 02:09:35,519
Take him.

1309
02:09:37,960 --> 02:09:41,399
Send a message to Beys.

1310
02:09:41,680 --> 02:09:45,639
-Everything will be revealed.
-Get up!

1311
02:09:47,720 --> 02:09:50,199
You said your way was separated from Ulugan.

1312
02:09:50,200 --> 02:09:53,199
But it's you who killed the
innocent people in the hidden tribe.

1313
02:09:53,240 --> 02:09:57,519
I'd rather lose my head than
bow to this treacherous hatun!

1314
02:09:57,680 --> 02:09:59,919
Don't worry. You will lose your heads.

1315
02:10:00,040 --> 02:10:02,319
The head to be lost today...

1316
02:10:03,920 --> 02:10:05,639
...will be this dog's head.

1317
02:10:05,960 --> 02:10:07,799
And then, Osman?

1318
02:10:08,160 --> 02:10:10,559
What do you think will happen then?

1319
02:10:11,280 --> 02:10:13,079
Don't worry.

1320
02:10:13,920 --> 02:10:16,559
You will be the next.

1321
02:10:17,560 --> 02:10:20,879
Turn around and see my power, Osman Bey.

1322
02:10:25,480 --> 02:10:30,759
You think you can stand against me
with a few alps and mindless Beys?

1323
02:10:32,280 --> 02:10:33,639
No.

1324
02:10:34,320 --> 02:10:36,439
You can't do this.

1325
02:10:37,400 --> 02:10:39,359
Game is over.

1326
02:10:39,760 --> 02:10:41,359
Let Ulugan go.

1327
02:10:43,880 --> 02:10:45,919
-Or...
Or what?

1328
02:10:46,160 --> 02:10:50,919
Or I won't kill only you
but also all of your kin!

1329
02:10:57,360 --> 02:11:01,239
I'll leave you lonely and desperate, Osman Bey.

1330
02:11:01,320 --> 02:11:05,639
I can be lonely but never mistaken.

1331
02:11:06,680 --> 02:11:08,359
Even if I die

1332
02:11:09,080 --> 02:11:12,719
...those who follow me
will never let you get away.

1333
02:11:13,640 --> 02:11:19,359
Tell me... Have we ever
let the evil ones get away?

1334
02:11:27,040 --> 02:11:29,439
Say your final words.

1335
02:11:29,680 --> 02:11:33,119
If you do this.

1336
02:11:33,840 --> 02:11:36,519
...you'll be wiped out.

1337
02:11:36,920 --> 02:11:41,599
Mongolians who destroyed
you even for a messenger...

1338
02:11:42,480 --> 02:11:47,879
...will wipe you out of the history
for their glorious commander Ulugan.

1339
02:11:54,160 --> 02:11:57,239
You came here and trampled on my land.

1340
02:11:58,640 --> 02:12:00,759
You and people like you.

1341
02:12:01,880 --> 02:12:08,279
Whoever comes after you
and messes with my nation...

1342
02:12:10,880 --> 02:12:13,519
...will live the same fate.